{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_cab11c7d51554b5aa6d1fdbb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tCreated-GMT: 2026-11-18 15:58:04 GMT\n2\tCreated-Local: 2026-11-18 22:58:04 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n3\tCoding-Agent: codex\n4\tSession-ID: 01a1ea51-a87d-7062-ae12-e6c1c169b48c\n5\tRole: VM Engineer (compiler provenance)\n6\tImplementers:\n7\t- Model: gpt-6.1-sol | Status: stopped on compiler divergence | Rationale: same-session r2 continuation\n8\t\n9\t# cc4 r2 — STOPPED on reproduced Dart replay divergence\n10\t\n11\tRole: VM Engineer (compiler provenance)\n12\tWorktree: `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc4`\n13\tBranch/base: `cc4-fourhost-equality` / `2687ab0cf03ebaa232be49a2333347d12a71d9a3`.\n14\tNo commits. No compiler/source implementation changed. The r1 findings remain\n15\tunchanged. This report and evidence are written in the authorized worktree;\n16\tthe orchestrator can mirror them to its checkout.\n17\t\n18\t## Verdict and required next round\n19\t\n20\t**FAIL: four-host replay equality.** Dart produces different canonical code\n21\tfor the argument-vector and lower-unit cohort members; C1 keys and instruction\n22\tprovenance therefore also differ. The focused failing test reproduces this.\n23\tPer the brief's binding STOP rule, cc4 does not fix the compiler, re-pin Dart,\n24\tnormalize generated code, or continue budget/acceptance execution after this\n25\tfailure. A compiler determinism repair needs a separately authorized round.\n26\tThe acceptance bundle remains blocked. D1 is dissolved per the owner's dispatch;\n27\tno durable-correspondence verification or D1 consumption is claimed.\n28\t\n29\tA second, independent blocker is J2's inherited manifest: four existing test\n30\tnamespaces are unlisted. The cc4 callsite inclusion is implemented, but the\n31\tlane refuses before launching a Jolt child. This is a failed required gate,\n32\tnot an accepted reader limitation or a green skip.\n33\t\n34\t## Concrete compiler defect and diverging artifacts\n35\t\n36\tAll eight inputs are the SAME `.cljc` source/form literals and options. The\n37\tsource fixtures include float `1.5`, `^:replay` metadata, destructuring-generated\n38\ttemporaries, repeated `(identity a)` subtrees, a macro constructing a twin call,\n39\twrapper/library/prelude surfaces, and separate supplied admission tokens.\n40\tNo host-specific source conditional occurs in the cohort itself.\n41\t\n42\t| Entry | Application occurrences | JVM and Node canonical root | Dart canonical root |\n43\t|---|---:|---|---|\n44\t| argument-vector | 263 on both | `:segment/blake3-a0f9c217122ce675d1b3cd5f899740d604ec35f801eac9a4960153cbcd91d699` | `:segment/blake3-02eac587af541bc180db4109b3accd5e3981a92eb5d1d00e63d6f12d74b484b0` |\n45\t| lower-unit | 256 on both | `:segment/blake3-44c06492b31348905205b1e1130c27aa1c769790010291ca223d3ab61bfa2775` | `:segment/blake3-9fe835e99e3afc3c2dc7639e7f26d1bcb8ab08445ded6b08aa8d3c78d01546fa` |\n46\t\n47\tFor argument-vector, the JVM C1 digest is\n48\t`82385d11b83bd1a6bd540cc80011ec88f23cf2e9a959fecfd604eff029a1ba2a`, Dart is\n49\t`a7f9b710743fa0572fc24817d41abfdab16f14ddeef266d31e783fc9dcc59c69`.\n50\tFor lower-unit, JVM is\n51\t`654c6a31726250f58550db88ce905fda869f3040b350e298da0aa73995b581ed`, Dart is\n52\t`73663cae54144b2ea36899e0f134fda95004a66e47812f44a517309a21970514`.\n53\tFull key-vector and instruction-provenance digests, expected/actual, are retained\n54\tin `test/resources/yang/clojure/cc4-replay-dart-divergences.edn`.\n55\t\n56\tRead-only comparison of the saved row maps isolates a bottommost difference:\n57\t`assoc` constructing the generated arity error map. Its arguments are:\n58\t\n59\t- JVM/Node: `{} :yin.vm.data/reason :arity :yin.k/argc (data/count dsg__av) :yin.k/fn 'replay`\n60\t- Dart: `{} :yin.vm.data/reason :arity :yin.k/fn 'replay :yin.k/argc (data/count dsg__av)`\n61\t\n62\tThe common operator row is `:variable assoc`. All seven child addresses exist\n63\tunchanged on both hosts; only the order of the final two key/value pairs differs.\n64\tThe resulting application addresses are respectively\n65\t`:segment/blake3-8598820bee9b622d827c7879729f60dad19244f9f9869ee693c1eaca58c1bb94`\n66\tand\n67\t`:segment/blake3-9a8f3a641f0e49b7381eccc74a1373b0d6bf97e954964587a449fcc2ee177e9b`.\n68\tArgument-vector has 494 unique rows on each host, 32 exclusive rows on each;\n69\tlower-unit has 499 each, 45 exclusive rows on each.\n70\t\n71\tLikely cause (inference from saved rows and read-only source inspection):\n72\t`arity-error-form` at `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1087` constructs a map with\n73\t`cond->`/`assoc`; `compile-constructed-collection` at `:302–323` emits\n74\t`(interleave (keys form) (vals form))` without a stable ordering rule. The map's\n75\thost iteration order therefore enters canonical application operands. No fix\n76\twas attempted; choosing the ordering/evaluation policy is outside cc4.\n77\tThe runtime meaning may be equivalent for this error map, but C1 replay requires\n78\tidentical code addresses, and this gate correctly fails it.\n79\t\n80\t## Pinned cohort and artifact checklist\n81\t\n82\t`replay-expectations` is literal recorded JVM data, not generated expectations\n83\ton each host. `replay-snapshot` hashes the **entire** canonical-byte-sorted\n84\toccurrence-key vector and C1 relation using Jing BLAKE3; it also pins all three\n85\tformats' reconstructed call-provenance together. There is no origin/name/path\n86\tnormalization. The macro entry additionally pins its entire producing log.\n87\t`jing/canonical-compare` supplies ordering, avoiding host printer order.\n88\tThe original r1 pin keeps a directly asserted complete eight-key vector too.\n89\t\n90\t| Producer / artifact | Pinned surfaces | A | Equality result |\n91\t|---|---|---:|---|\n92\t| native `compile-program` | root, full C1/keys, semantic/stack/register provenance | 14 | JVM/Node/Dart match |\n93\t| `compile-program` with `true yang/unit-opts` | same, including generated arity helper | 263 | JVM/Node match; Dart diverges |\n94\t| `lower-unit` | wrappers + bundled `library-for`, all C1/keys/provenance | 256 | JVM/Node match; Dart diverges |\n95\t| `clj-prelude/module-uast` | root and complete static relations | 114 | JVM/Node/Dart match |\n96\t| production macro expansion | constructed/retained twin origins, full producing log | 5 | JVM/Node/Dart match |\n97\t| second supplied admission token | same native root, different full origins/keys | 14 | JVM/Node/Dart match |\n98\t| fresh `yang.call` publication | root, full C1/keys, table/provenance/record/manifest addresses | 100 | JVM/Node/Dart match |\n99\t| fresh `clj` publication | same complete side artifacts and dependency address | 114 | JVM/Node/Dart match |\n100\t\n101\tTotal A = 880, including duplicate admissions and shared prelude content.\n102\tThis is an occurrence count, not a storage-deduplicated count. The negative fixture\n103\tuses supplied `\"admission-a\"` and `\"admission-b\"` on `:cc4/replay`, member 0;\n104\troots match and origin sets differ. Macro coordinates are supplied by the existing\n105\tproduction-style helper: seed token/medium `:callsite-test/standard-forms`,\n106\tprogram token `\"callsite-test\"`, medium `:program-in`, initial t=0. Expansion\n107\trecords and their producing chain are included verbatim in the log digest.\n108\tPublication uses the publisher's recorded deterministic default specification\n109\tadmission; its real origins are included in the complete C1/key digests.\n110\t`:origin` is omitted only from the redundant address-summary map, because its\n111\tprinted keyword is not EDN-reader-safe; no persisted origin is changed.\n112\t\n113\tNative uses default opts; the argument-vector and linked unit use the dispatch\n114\trevision's `yang/unit-opts`: convention `:arg-vector`, `:outcomes true`,\n115\t`:linked-runtime true`, `library-adapters`, and `vm/primitive-profiles`.\n116\tThose historical option names remain as implemented after