{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_e8079c85d3854b308bb44a9b","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t(ns yin.repl.frontends\n2\t  \"The REPL's standard frontend catalog (docs/design/yang.antlr.md section\n3\t   8.5.6, slice F2): the hand-written Clojure frontend and the ANTLR PHP and\n4\t   Python frontends installed into a `yang.frontend` catalog. This is\n5\t   the only place the REPL composition names a language's namespace;\n6\t   `yin.repl` core steps whatever binding the catalog selects.\n7\t\n8\t   A binding is `{:parse (fn [input]) :lower (fn [parsed])}`, with\n9\t   `:input :forms` when the frontend consumes the forms the shell reader\n10\t   already read, else the source text.\"\n11\t  (:require\n12\t    [yang.clojure :as yang.clojure]\n13\t    [yang.frontend :as frontend]\n14\t    #?@(:cljd []\n15\t        :jolt []\n16\t        :default [[yang.php.antlr.cst :as php.antlr.cst]\n17\t                  [yang.php.antlr.lower :as php.antlr.lower]])\n18\t    #?@(:cljd [[yang.python.antlr.repl :as python.antlr.repl]\n19\t               [yang.python.antlr.parser :as python.antlr.parser]\n20\t               [yang.python.antlr.repl-probe :as python.antlr.probe]]\n21\t        :default [[yang.python.antlr.repl :as python.antlr.repl]\n22\t                  [yang.python.antlr.parser :as python.antlr.parser]\n23\t                  [yang.python.antlr.repl-probe :as python.antlr.probe]])\n24\t    [yin.repl :as repl]))\n25\t\n26\t\n27\t(defn- manifest\n28\t  [id language]\n29\t  {:yang.frontend/id id,\n30\t   :yang.frontend/spi 1,\n31\t   :yang.frontend/revision \"legacy-1\",\n32\t   :yang.frontend/language language,\n33\t   :yang.frontend/grammar {:yang.grammar/package \"none\",\n34\t                           :yang.grammar/entries {:module \"program\"},\n35\t                           :yang.grammar/export-profile :yang.cst/v1},\n36\t   :yang.frontend/options-schema :segment/none,\n37\t   :yang.frontend/lowering-profile :segment/legacy,\n38\t   :yang.frontend/runtime-profile :segment/legacy,\n39\t   :yang.frontend/support-profile :segment/legacy})\n40\t\n41\t\n42\t(defn clojure-manifest\n43\t  \"The Clojure frontend's manifest. Its coverage promise changed under\n44\t   the call-site occurrence contract C1 — every final `:application`\n45\t   occurrence carries `:yang/call-site` in the frontend-metadata side\n46\t   table, finalized over the post-expansion tree that executes and\n47\t   retained beside a published module's manifest — and that promise is\n48\t   a support claim, so the revision and the support profile name it;\n49\t   the shared legacy profiles no longer describe this frontend.\"\n50\t  []\n51\t  (assoc (manifest :yang/clojure :clojure)\n52\t         :yang.frontend/revision \"c1-1\"\n53\t         :yang.frontend/support-profile :yang.clojure/c1))\n54\t\n55\t\n56\t(defn- clojure-lower\n57\t  [forms]\n58\t  (if (= 1 (count forms))\n59\t    (yang.clojure/compile (first forms))\n60\t    (yang.clojure/compile-program forms)))\n61\t\n62\t\n63\t(defn- antlr-manifest\n64\t  []\n65\t  (assoc (manifest :yang/python :python)\n66\t         :yang.frontend/revision \"f4\"\n67\t         :yang.frontend/grammar\n68\t         {:yang.grammar/package \"python3\",\n69\t          :yang.grammar/entries {:module \"file_input\"},\n70\t          :yang.grammar/export-profile :yang.cst/v1,\n71\t          :yang.grammar/targets #{:java :javascript :dart}}))\n72\t\n73\t\n74\t(defn php-manifest\n75\t  []\n76\t  (assoc (manifest :yang/php :php)\n77\t         :yang.frontend/revision \"antlr-p8\"\n78\t         :yang.frontend/grammar\n79\t         {:yang.grammar/package \"php\",\n80\t          :yang.grammar/entries {:module \"htmlDocument\"},"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"e5138865-ad00-4622-9c41-826273fe679f","timestamp":"2026-11-18T16:15:41.013Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-fixorder/src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc","content":"(ns yin.repl.frontends\n  \"The REPL's standard frontend catalog (docs/design/yang.antlr.md section\n   8.5.6, slice F2): the hand-written Clojure frontend and the ANTLR PHP and\n   Python frontends installed into a `yang.frontend` catalog. This is\n   the only place the REPL composition names a language's namespace;\n   `yin.repl` core steps whatever binding the catalog selects.\n\n   A binding is `{:parse (fn [input]) :lower (fn [parsed])}`, with\n   `:input :forms` when the frontend consumes the forms the shell reader\n   already read, else the source text.\"\n  (:require\n    [yang.clojure :as yang.clojure]\n    [yang.frontend :as frontend]\n    #?@(:cljd []\n        :jolt []\n        :default [[yang.php.antlr.cst :as php.antlr.cst]\n                  [yang.php.antlr.lower :as php.antlr.lower]])\n    #?@(:cljd [[yang.python.antlr.repl :as python.antlr.repl]\n               [yang.python.antlr.parser :as python.antlr.parser]\n               [yang.python.antlr.repl-probe :as python.antlr.probe]]\n        :default [[yang.python.antlr.repl :as python.antlr.repl]\n                  [yang.python.antlr.parser :as python.antlr.parser]\n                  [yang.python.antlr.repl-probe :as python.antlr.probe]])\n    [yin.repl :as repl]))\n\n\n(defn- manifest\n  [id language]\n  {:yang.frontend/id id,\n   :yang.frontend/spi 1,\n   :yang.frontend/revision \"legacy-1\",\n   :yang.frontend/language language,\n   :yang.frontend/grammar {:yang.grammar/package \"none\",\n                           :yang.grammar/entries {:module \"program\"},\n                           :yang.grammar/export-profile :yang.cst/v1},\n   :yang.frontend/options-schema :segment/none,\n   :yang.frontend/lowering-profile :segment/legacy,\n   :yang.frontend/runtime-profile :segment/legacy,\n   :yang.frontend/support-profile :segment/legacy})\n\n\n(defn clojure-manifest\n  \"The Clojure frontend's manifest. Its coverage promise changed under\n   the call-site occurrence contract C1 — every final `:application`\n   occurrence carries `:yang/call-site` in the frontend-metadata side\n   table, finalized over the post-expansion tree that executes and\n   retained beside a published module's manifest — and that promise is\n   a support claim, so the revision and the support profile name it;\n   the shared legacy profiles no longer describe this frontend.\"\n  []\n  (assoc (manifest :yang/clojure :clojure)\n         :yang.frontend/revision \"c1-1\"\n         :yang.frontend/support-profile :yang.clojure/c1))\n\n\n(defn- clojure-lower\n  [forms]\n  (if (= 1 (count forms))\n    (yang.clojure/compile (first forms))\n    (yang.clojure/compile-program forms)))\n\n\n(defn- antlr-manifest\n  []\n  (assoc (manifest :yang/python :python)\n         :yang.frontend/revision \"f4\"\n         :yang.frontend/grammar\n         {:yang.grammar/package \"python3\",\n          :yang.grammar/entries {:module \"file_input\"},\n          :yang.grammar/export-profile :yang.cst/v1,\n          :yang.grammar/targets #{:java :javascript :dart}}))\n\n\n(defn php-manifest\n  []\n  (assoc (manifest :yang/php :php)\n         :yang.frontend/revision \"antlr-p8\"\n         :yang.frontend/grammar\n         {:yang.grammar/package \"php\",\n          :yang.grammar/entries {:module \"htmlDocument\"},","numLines":80,"startLine":1,"totalLines":155}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"call_e8079c85d3854b308bb44a9b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
