{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_1db1ecc349c24a6c90c8c546","type":"tool_result","content":"160\t    :blake3 (blake3-bytes bs)\n161\t    :sha256 (sha256-bytes bs)\n162\t    (throw (ex-info (str \"unsupported hash algorithm: \" algorithm)\n163\t                    {:algorithm algorithm}))))\n164\t\n165\t\n166\t(defn digest-string\n167\t  \"Digest string s as UTF-8 bytes with the specified algorithm keyword.\n168\t   Returns lowercase hexadecimal string. Unknown algorithms throw.\"\n169\t  [algorithm s]\n170\t  (case algorithm\n171\t    :blake3 (blake3 s)\n172\t    :sha256 (sha256 s)\n173\t    (throw (ex-info (str \"unsupported hash algorithm: \" algorithm)\n174\t                    {:algorithm algorithm}))))\n175\t\n176\t\n177\t(defn canonical-bytes\n178\t  \"Return the deterministic CBOR bytes (byte[] / Uint8Array / Uint8List)\n179\t   of v -- the exact bytes content hashing digests, so\n180\t   `(digest-bytes algo (canonical-bytes v))` is\n181\t   `(content-hash v {:algorithm algo})`.\n182\t   This is the byte form Jing content travels in across a `dao.stream`\n183\t   boundary.\"\n184\t  [v]\n185\t  (cbor/encode v))\n186\t\n187\t\n188\t(defn canonical-compare\n189\t  \"Total order over values by their canonical bytes: unsigned bytewise\n190\t   lexicographic order over `(canonical-bytes v)`, a proper prefix\n191\t   sorting first (RFC 8949 canonical order). Host-independent, unlike\n192\t   ordering by `pr-str`, whose rendering is a host's printer.\"\n193\t  [a b]\n194\t  (let [x (canonical-bytes a)\n195\t        y (canonical-bytes b)\n196\t        nx (bytes/length x)\n197\t        ny (bytes/length y)\n198\t        n (min nx ny)]\n199\t    (loop [i 0]\n200\t      (if (< i n)\n201\t        (let [bx (bytes/get x i)\n202\t              by (bytes/get y i)]\n203\t          (if (= bx by)\n204\t            (recur (inc i))\n205\t            (if (< bx by) -1 1)))\n206\t        (cond\n207\t          (< nx ny) -1\n208\t          (> nx ny) 1\n209\t          :else 0)))))\n210\t\n211\t\n212\t(defn content-hash\n213\t  \"Hash the canonical-bytes of v using the specified algorithm (defaulting to\n214\t   default-hash-algorithm, i.e. :blake3). Returns lowercase hexadecimal string.\n215\t   Arities: [v] and [v {:keys [algorithm]}].\"\n216\t  ([v]\n217\t   (content-hash v {:algorithm default-hash-algorithm}))\n218\t  ([v opts]\n219\t   (let [algo (clojure.core/get opts :algorithm default-hash-algorithm)]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"f511b349-076d-4445-9c22-6250a79acc23","timestamp":"2026-11-18T16:15:44.200Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-fixorder/src/cljc/dao/jing.cljc","content":"    :blake3 (blake3-bytes bs)\n    :sha256 (sha256-bytes bs)\n    (throw (ex-info (str \"unsupported hash algorithm: \" algorithm)\n                    {:algorithm algorithm}))))\n\n\n(defn digest-string\n  \"Digest string s as UTF-8 bytes with the specified algorithm keyword.\n   Returns lowercase hexadecimal string. Unknown algorithms throw.\"\n  [algorithm s]\n  (case algorithm\n    :blake3 (blake3 s)\n    :sha256 (sha256 s)\n    (throw (ex-info (str \"unsupported hash algorithm: \" algorithm)\n                    {:algorithm algorithm}))))\n\n\n(defn canonical-bytes\n  \"Return the deterministic CBOR bytes (byte[] / Uint8Array / Uint8List)\n   of v -- the exact bytes content hashing digests, so\n   `(digest-bytes algo (canonical-bytes v))` is\n   `(content-hash v {:algorithm algo})`.\n   This is the byte form Jing content travels in across a `dao.stream`\n   boundary.\"\n  [v]\n  (cbor/encode v))\n\n\n(defn canonical-compare\n  \"Total order over values by their canonical bytes: unsigned bytewise\n   lexicographic order over `(canonical-bytes v)`, a proper prefix\n   sorting first (RFC 8949 canonical order). Host-independent, unlike\n   ordering by `pr-str`, whose rendering is a host's printer.\"\n  [a b]\n  (let [x (canonical-bytes a)\n        y (canonical-bytes b)\n        nx (bytes/length x)\n        ny (bytes/length y)\n        n (min nx ny)]\n    (loop [i 0]\n      (if (< i n)\n        (let [bx (bytes/get x i)\n              by (bytes/get y i)]\n          (if (= bx by)\n            (recur (inc i))\n            (if (< bx by) -1 1)))\n        (cond\n          (< nx ny) -1\n          (> nx ny) 1\n          :else 0)))))\n\n\n(defn content-hash\n  \"Hash the canonical-bytes of v using the specified algorithm (defaulting to\n   default-hash-algorithm, i.e. :blake3). Returns lowercase hexadecimal string.\n   Arities: [v] and [v {:keys [algorithm]}].\"\n  ([v]\n   (content-hash v {:algorithm default-hash-algorithm}))\n  ([v opts]\n   (let [algo (clojure.core/get opts :algorithm default-hash-algorithm)]","numLines":60,"startLine":160,"totalLines":671}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"call_1db1ecc349c24a6c90c8c546","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
