{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_f763e23f0ab34aee9e23f420","type":"tool_result","content":"1140\t                                          (let [[k' v'] (find b k)]\n1141\t                                            (and (same-content? k k')\n1142\t                                                 (same-content? v v')))))\n1143\t                                   a))\n1144\t             (set? a) (and (set? b)\n1145\t                           (= (count a) (count b))\n1146\t                           (every? (fn [e]\n1147\t                                     (same-content? e (some #(when (= e %) %) b)))\n1148\t                                   a))\n1149\t             (sequential? a) (and (sequential? b)\n1150\t                                  (= (count a) (count b))\n1151\t                                  (every? true? (map same-content? a b)))\n1152\t             :else (cbor/content= a b))))\n1153\t\n1154\t\n1155\t(defn ast->semantic-bytecode\n1156\t  \"Project a map AST to flat content-addressed rows (§6.1 codec boundary\n1157\t   projection). Returns `{:root row-id, :rows {row-id [row-id tag & slots]}}`.\n1158\t\n1159\t   Only the §2.3 slots of each node enter its row: `:eid`, `:macro?`,\n1160\t   `:yang/*` keys, non-`:application` `:tail?` marks, and any other key are\n1161\t   dropped. `sym`/`syms` slots lose all metadata; `data`/`key` payloads lose\n1162\t   reader positions at every depth and keep all other metadata. Defaults are\n1163\t   saturated per §2.4. Children are projected first, so a parent's body\n1164\t   commits to its children's ids; structurally identical subtrees mint one\n1165\t   id and are stored as one row (§4.4).\n1166\t\n1167\t   Two nodes that mint one id must have one content: the row is checked\n1168\t   against the stored row with `same-content?` (metadata at every depth,\n1169\t   leaves by `dao.jing.cbor/content=`), and a mismatch throws\n1170\t   \\\"Semantic bytecode address collision\\\" rather than letting one row silently\n1171\t   replace the other. No known input reaches that throw: the encoder hashes\n1172\t   symbol and collection metadata, and makes every NaN one quiet NaN, so two\n1173\t   NaN scalars are one row value. The guard is a defence against the encoder\n1174\t   and this check disagreeing.\"\n1175\t  [ast]\n1176\t  (let [rows (atom {})]\n1177\t    (letfn\n1178\t      [(slot-value\n1179\t         [tag node [field kind]]\n1180\t         (let [v (get node field)\n1181\t               v (if (nil? v) (get semantic-bytecode-defaults [tag field]) v)]\n1182\t           (case kind\n1183\t             :node (convert v)\n1184\t             :nodes (mapv convert v)\n1185\t             :sym (strip-symbol-meta v)\n1186\t             :syms (mapv strip-symbol-meta v)\n1187\t             :bool (boolean v)\n1188\t             (:data :key) (strip-reader-positions v)\n1189\t             v)))\n1190\t       (convert\n1191\t         [node]\n1192\t         (let [tag (:type node)\n1193\t               slots (or (get semantic-bytecode-grammar tag)\n1194\t                         (throw (ex-info \"Unknown AST node type\"\n1195\t                                         {:type tag, :node node})))\n1196\t               body (into [tag] (map #(slot-value tag node %)) slots)\n1197\t               id (jing/segment-key body)\n1198\t               row (into [id] body)\n1199\t               prior (get @rows id)]\n1200\t           (when (and prior\n1201\t                      (not (same-content? prior row)))\n1202\t             (throw (ex-info \"Semantic bytecode address collision\"\n1203\t                             {:id id, :row row, :prior prior})))\n1204\t           (swap! rows assoc id row)\n1205\t           id))]\n1206\t      (let [root (convert ast)]\n1207\t        {:root root, :rows @rows}))))\n1208\t\n1209\t\n1210\t(def ^:private source-position-keys\n1211\t  #{:file :line :column :end-line :end-column})\n1212\t\n1213\t\n1214\t(defn- reader-position\n1215\t  [node]\n1216\t  (let [source (:yang/source-position node)\n1217\t        m (meta node)\n1218\t        value (merge (select-keys m source-position-keys)\n1219\t                     (select-keys node source-position-keys)\n1220\t                     (when (map? source) source))]\n1221\t    (when (some #(contains? value %) [:file :line :column])\n1222\t      value)))\n1223\t\n1224\t\n1225\t(defn- frontend-meta-entries\n1226\t  \"Ordered `[key value]` entries attached to one Universal AST node. Yang\n1227\t   keys and non-position map metadata are node facts. Reader metadata on a\n1228\t   name or parameter is qualified by its semantic field so two parameters\n1229\t   cannot silently claim the same key at one lambda occurrence.\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"5e94b32a-179b-48f7-aa62-28a974cd3704","timestamp":"2026-11-18T16:15:47.135Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-fixorder/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc","content":"                                          (let [[k' v'] (find b k)]\n                                            (and (same-content? k k')\n                                                 (same-content? v v')))))\n                                   a))\n             (set? a) (and (set? b)\n                           (= (count a) (count b))\n                           (every? (fn [e]\n                                     (same-content? e (some #(when (= e %) %) b)))\n                                   a))\n             (sequential? a) (and (sequential? b)\n                                  (= (count a) (count b))\n                                  (every? true? (map same-content? a b)))\n             :else (cbor/content= a b))))\n\n\n(defn ast->semantic-bytecode\n  \"Project a map AST to flat content-addressed rows (§6.1 codec boundary\n   projection). Returns `{:root row-id, :rows {row-id [row-id tag & slots]}}`.\n\n   Only the §2.3 slots of each node enter its row: `:eid`, `:macro?`,\n   `:yang/*` keys, non-`:application` `:tail?` marks, and any other key are\n   dropped. `sym`/`syms` slots lose all metadata; `data`/`key` payloads lose\n   reader positions at every depth and keep all other metadata. Defaults are\n   saturated per §2.4. Children are projected first, so a parent's body\n   commits to its children's ids; structurally identical subtrees mint one\n   id and are stored as one row (§4.4).\n\n   Two nodes that mint one id must have one content: the row is checked\n   against the stored row with `same-content?` (metadata at every depth,\n   leaves by `dao.jing.cbor/content=`), and a mismatch throws\n   \\\"Semantic bytecode address collision\\\" rather than letting one row silently\n   replace the other. No known input reaches that throw: the encoder hashes\n   symbol and collection metadata, and makes every NaN one quiet NaN, so two\n   NaN scalars are one row value. The guard is a defence against the encoder\n   and this check disagreeing.\"\n  [ast]\n  (let [rows (atom {})]\n    (letfn\n      [(slot-value\n         [tag node [field kind]]\n         (let [v (get node field)\n               v (if (nil? v) (get semantic-bytecode-defaults [tag field]) v)]\n           (case kind\n             :node (convert v)\n             :nodes (mapv convert v)\n             :sym (strip-symbol-meta v)\n             :syms (mapv strip-symbol-meta v)\n             :bool (boolean v)\n             (:data :key) (strip-reader-positions v)\n             v)))\n       (convert\n         [node]\n         (let [tag (:type node)\n               slots (or (get semantic-bytecode-grammar tag)\n                         (throw (ex-info \"Unknown AST node type\"\n                                         {:type tag, :node node})))\n               body (into [tag] (map #(slot-value tag node %)) slots)\n               id (jing/segment-key body)\n               row (into [id] body)\n               prior (get @rows id)]\n           (when (and prior\n                      (not (same-content? prior row)))\n             (throw (ex-info \"Semantic bytecode address collision\"\n                             {:id id, :row row, :prior prior})))\n           (swap! rows assoc id row)\n           id))]\n      (let [root (convert ast)]\n        {:root root, :rows @rows}))))\n\n\n(def ^:private source-position-keys\n  #{:file :line :column :end-line :end-column})\n\n\n(defn- reader-position\n  [node]\n  (let [source (:yang/source-position node)\n        m (meta node)\n        value (merge (select-keys m source-position-keys)\n                     (select-keys node source-position-keys)\n                     (when (map? source) source))]\n    (when (some #(contains? value %) [:file :line :column])\n      value)))\n\n\n(defn- frontend-meta-entries\n  \"Ordered `[key value]` entries attached to one Universal AST node. Yang\n   keys and non-position map metadata are node facts. Reader metadata on a\n   name or parameter is qualified by its semantic field so two parameters\n   cannot silently claim the same key at one lambda occurrence.\"","numLines":90,"startLine":1140,"totalLines":2202}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"call_f763e23f0ab34aee9e23f420","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
