{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_0147924afc2749dfa4189200","type":"tool_result","content":"1567\t(defn compile-application\n1568\t  \"Compile a function application to Universal AST.\n1569\t\n1570\t  Clojure: (+ 1 2)\n1571\t  AST: {:type :application\n1572\t        :operator <compiled-operator>\n1573\t        :operands [<compiled-operand1> <compiled-operand2>]}\n1574\t\n1575\t  Under the argument-vector convention a user-function call passes its\n1576\t  operands as one vector.\"\n1577\t  ([operator operands env tail?] (compile-application operator operands env tail? initial-macro-env))\n1578\t  ([operator operands env tail? macro-env]\n1579\t   (if (and (::convention env) (not (macro-call? env macro-env operator)))\n1580\t     (compile-av-application operator operands env tail? macro-env)\n1581\t     (let [compiled-operator (compile-form operator false env macro-env)\n1582\t           compiled-operands (mapv #(compile-form % false env macro-env) operands)]\n1583\t       (cond-> {:type :application,\n1584\t                :operator compiled-operator,\n1585\t                :operands compiled-operands}\n1586\t         tail? (assoc :tail? true))))))\n1587\t\n1588\t\n1589\t(defn compile-dao-stream-apply-call\n1590\t  \"Compile a dao.stream.apply call form to Universal AST.\n1591\t\n1592\t  Clojure: (dao.stream.apply/call :op/name arg1 arg2)\n1593\t  AST: {:type :dao.stream.apply/call\n1594\t        :op :op/name\n1595\t        :operands [<compiled-arg1> <compiled-arg2>]}\"\n1596\t  ([op operands env tail?] (compile-dao-stream-apply-call op operands env tail? initial-macro-env))\n1597\t  ([op operands env tail? macro-env]\n1598\t   (when-not (keyword? op)\n1599\t     (throw (ex-info \"dao.stream.apply/call op must be a keyword\" {:op op})))\n1600\t   (let [compiled-operands (mapv #(compile-form % false env macro-env) operands)]\n1601\t     (cond-> {:type :dao.stream.apply/call,\n1602\t              :op op,\n1603\t              :operands compiled-operands}\n1604\t       tail? (assoc :tail? true)))))\n1605\t\n1606\t\n1607\t(defn compile-if\n1608\t  \"Compile a conditional (if) expression to Universal AST.\n1609\t\n1610\t  Clojure: (if test consequent alternate)\n1611\t  AST: {:type :if\n1612\t        :test <compiled-test>\n1613\t        :consequent <compiled-consequent>\n1614\t        :alternate <compiled-alternate>}\n1615\t\n1616\t  An explicit `false` alternate is a value, not an absence: `alternate-present?`\n1617\t  distinguishes (if t c) from (if t c false).\"\n1618\t  ([test consequent alternate env tail?]\n1619\t   (compile-if test consequent alternate true env tail? initial-macro-env))\n1620\t  ([test consequent alternate alt-present? env tail?]\n1621\t   (compile-if test consequent alternate alt-present? env tail? initial-macro-env))\n1622\t  ([test consequent alternate alt-present? env tail? macro-env]\n1623\t   (cond-> {:type :if,\n1624\t            :test (compile-form test false env macro-env),\n1625\t            :consequent (compile-form consequent tail? env macro-env),\n1626\t            :alternate (if alt-present?\n1627\t                         (compile-form alternate tail? env macro-env)\n1628\t                         (compile-literal nil tail?))}\n1629\t     tail? (assoc :tail? true))))\n1630\t\n1631\t\n1632\t(declare compile-let-simple)\n1633\t\n1634\t\n1635\t(defn compile-let\n1636\t  \"Compile a let binding to Universal AST.\n1637\t\n1638\t  Transforms let into nested lambda applications:\n1639\t  (let [x 1 y 2] (+ x y))\n1640\t  =>\n1641\t  ((fn [x] ((fn [y] (+ x y)) 2)) 1)\"\n1642\t  ([bindings body env tail?] (compile-let bindings body env tail? initial-macro-env))\n1643\t  ([bindings body env tail? macro-env]\n1644\t   (compile-let-simple (expand-bindings bindings env) body env tail? macro-env)))\n1645\t\n1646\t\n1647\t(defn- compile-let-simple\n1648\t  \"compile-let over a binding vector whose targets are all plain symbols.\"\n1649\t  [bindings body env tail? macro-env