{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_7dde938b491a46d988bd98d2","type":"tool_result","content":"1940\t\n1941\t  Quoted forms become literals.\"\n1942\t  [form tail?]\n1943\t  (compile-literal form tail?))\n1944\t\n1945\t\n1946\t(defn resolve-primitive\n1947\t  \"Resolve primitive operations in the environment.\n1948\t\n1949\t  Primitives like +, -, *, /, =, <, > are built into the Yin VM\n1950\t  and are accessed as variables.\"\n1951\t  [sym]\n1952\t  (when (contains? #{'+ '- '* '/ '= '< '>} sym) sym))\n1953\t\n1954\t\n1955\t(defn- compile-form*\n1956\t  \"Compile a Clojure form to Universal AST.\n1957\t\n1958\t  This is the main entry point that dispatches to specific compilers\n1959\t  based on the form type.\n1960\t\n1961\t  macro-env: compile-time map of defmacro names in scope. A macro call is an\n1962\t  ordinary application; macro-env only stops the native defn lowering.\"\n1963\t  [form tail? env macro-env top?]\n1964\t  (cond\n1965\t    ;; Literals: constants self-evaluate; collections with dynamic elements\n1966\t    ;; lower to constructor calls so their elements evaluate like Clojure\n1967\t    (literal? form)\n1968\t    (if (constant-form? form)\n1969\t      (compile-literal form tail?)\n1970\t      (compile-constructed-collection form tail? env macro-env))\n1971\t    ;; The empty list is self-evaluating data, not an application\n1972\t    (and (seq? form) (empty? form)) (compile-literal form tail?)\n1973\t    ;; Variables (symbols)\n1974\t    (symbol? form) (if (native-name? env form)\n1975\t                     (if (outcomes? env)\n1976\t                       (compile-call-descriptor (compile-adapter form env false macro-env) tail?)\n1977\t                       (compile-adapter form env tail? macro-env))\n1978\t                     (compile-variable form tail?))\n1979\t    ;; Special forms and function application\n1980\t    (seq? form)\n1981\t    (let [[operator & operands] form]\n1982\t      (cond\n1983\t        ;; dao.stream.apply call: (dao.stream.apply/call :op/name arg1 arg2)\n1984\t        (= operator 'dao.stream.apply/call)\n1985\t        (let [[op & args] operands]\n1986\t          (compile-dao-stream-apply-call op args env tail? macro-env))\n1987\t        ;; Native defn fallback: used only when no defmacro defn is in scope\n1988\t        ;; and the form actually matches defn syntax.\n1989\t        (and (contains? #{'defn 'defn-} operator)\n1990\t             (not (contains? macro-env operator)))\n1991\t        (do (check-top-level! env top? operator)\n1992\t            (compile-defn operator operands env tail? macro-env))\n1993\t\n1994\t        ;; Special forms\n1995\t        :else\n1996\t        (case operator\n1997\t          ;; Lambda: (fn [params] body)\n1998\t          fn (if (::convention env)\n1999\t               (compile-av-fn (fn-arities operands) env tail? macro-env nil (source-meta form))\n2000\t               (let [[params & body] operands]\n2001\t                 (compile-fn params body env tail? macro-env)))\n2002\t          ;; Compiler-internal raw lambda (the continuation family's thunks):\n2003\t          ;; a plain closure, never the convention's published descriptor.\n2004\t          dsg__raw-fn (let [[params & body] operands]\n2005\t                        (compile-lambda params (body-expression body)\n2006\t                                        env false macro-env))\n2007\t          ;; Conditional: (if test consequent alternate?)\n2008\t          if (let [[test consequent alternate] operands]\n2009\t               (compile-if test consequent alternate (> (count operands) 2) env tail? macro-env))\n2010\t          ;; Let binding: (let [bindings] body)\n2011\t          let (let [[bindings & body] operands\n2012\t                    body-expr (if (= 1 (count body)) (first body) (cons 'do body))]\n2013\t                (compile-let bindings body-expr env tail? macro-env))\n2014\t          ;; Do block: (do expr1 expr2 ...)\n2015\t          do (compile-do operands env tail? macro-env)\n2016\t          loop (compile-loop operands env tail? macro-env (::fn-loop (meta form)))\n2017\t          ;; Internal let whose bindings are already lowered.\n2018\t          dsg__let (compile-let-simple (first operands) (body-expression (rest operands))\n2019\t                                       env tail? macro-env)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"d4d3cd08-ba5a-46fb-87ad-d54e208863ec","timestamp":"2026-11-18T16:17:26.227Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-fixorder/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc","content":"\n  Quoted forms become literals.\"\n  [form tail?]\n  (compile-literal form tail?))\n\n\n(defn resolve-primitive\n  \"Resolve primitive operations in the environment.\n\n  Primitives like +, -, *, /, =, <, > are built into the Yin VM\n  and are accessed as variables.\"\n  [sym]\n  (when (contains? #{'+ '- '* '/ '= '< '>} sym) sym))\n\n\n(defn- compile-form*\n  \"Compile a Clojure form to Universal AST.\n\n  This is the main entry point that dispatches to specific compilers\n  based on the form type.\n\n  macro-env: compile-time map of defmacro names in scope. A macro call is an\n  ordinary application; macro-env only stops the native defn lowering.\"\n  [form tail? env macro-env top?]\n  (cond\n    ;; Literals: constants self-evaluate; collections with dynamic elements\n    ;; lower to constructor calls so their elements evaluate like Clojure\n    (literal? form)\n    (if (constant-form? form)\n      (compile-literal form tail?)\n      (compile-constructed-collection form tail? env macro-env))\n    ;; The empty list is self-evaluating data, not an application\n    (and (seq? form) (empty? form)) (compile-literal form tail?)\n    ;; Variables (symbols)\n    (symbol? form) (if (native-name? env form)\n                     (if (outcomes? env)\n                       (compile-call-descriptor (compile-adapter form env false macro-env) tail?)\n                       (compile-adapter form env tail? macro-env))\n                     (compile-variable form tail?))\n    ;; Special forms and function application\n    (seq? form)\n    (let [[operator & operands] form]\n      (cond\n        ;; dao.stream.apply call: (dao.stream.apply/call :op/name arg1 arg2)\n        (= operator 'dao.stream.apply/call)\n        (let [[op & args] operands]\n          (compile-dao-stream-apply-call op args env tail? macro-env))\n        ;; Native defn fallback: used only when no defmacro defn is in scope\n        ;; and the form actually matches defn syntax.\n        (and (contains? #{'defn 'defn-} operator)\n             (not (contains? macro-env operator)))\n        (do (check-top-level! env top? operator)\n            (compile-defn operator operands env tail? macro-env))\n\n        ;; Special forms\n        :else\n        (case operator\n          ;; Lambda: (fn [params] body)\n          fn (if (::convention env)\n               (compile-av-fn (fn-arities operands) env tail? macro-env nil (source-meta form))\n               (let [[params & body] operands]\n                 (compile-fn params body env tail? macro-env)))\n          ;; Compiler-internal raw lambda (the continuation family's thunks):\n          ;; a plain closure, never the convention's published descriptor.\n          dsg__raw-fn (let [[params & body] operands]\n                        (compile-lambda params (body-expression body)\n                                        env false macro-env))\n          ;; Conditional: (if test consequent alternate?)\n          if (let [[test consequent alternate] operands]\n               (compile-if test consequent alternate (> (count operands) 2) env tail? macro-env))\n          ;; Let binding: (let [bindings] body)\n          let (let [[bindings & body] operands\n                    body-expr (if (= 1 (count body)) (first body) (cons 'do body))]\n                (compile-let bindings body-expr env tail? macro-env))\n          ;; Do block: (do expr1 expr2 ...)\n          do (compile-do operands env tail? macro-env)\n          loop (compile-loop operands env tail? macro-env (::fn-loop (meta form)))\n          ;; Internal let whose bindings are already lowered.\n          dsg__let (compile-let-simple (first operands) (body-expression (rest operands))\n                                       env tail? macro-env)","numLines":80,"startLine":1940,"totalLines":3122}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"call_7dde938b491a46d988bd98d2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
