{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20261119002055d50bb6ddce8b4998","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK — `test_utils.cljc` is portable (`test/yin/vm/test_utils.cljc`). It gives:\n- walker lane: `make-observer-session` + `queue-ast!` + `run-session` → `vm/value`\n- row/semantic lane: `queue-rows!` (loads `ast->semantic-bytecode` row set) — this goes through the same walker? Actually `queue-rows!` queues rows as program batch; then the VM's loader... Hmm, for row sets the evaluator uses semantic/load-vector via `engine`. Let me look at `run-session` and how run-encoder-session is used — `make-encoder-session` requires `dao.stream` (clj only?). The ns header of test_utils: let me check reader conditionals — `make-stream` uses `stream/make`... `dao.stream` might be :clj-only. The callsite test gates `dao.stream` requires with `#?@(:clj ...)`. But test_utils.cljc is used by clojure_test.clj (a .clj test, JVM only) — is test_utils portable to cljs/cljd? Let me check its ns form and whether `dao.stream` is available on all hosts.","signature":"eefbb7ef8d184052a74ad352"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"8601c047-fea1-4937-ae52-8a004236dc0a","timestamp":"2026-11-18T16:21:01.955Z","thinking_duration_ms":3843,"thinking_display":"updates"}
