{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_c5bedbc1343b4109ac701251","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t(ns yin.vm.test-utils\n2\t  \"Composition helpers for the v2 VM suite.\n3\t\n4\t   Every v2 test supplies `:make-stream`: the VM has no default transport, so\n5\t   a test that omits it gets a VM that cannot create streams. The ring buffer\n6\t   is the composition's choice here, not the VM's.\n7\t\n8\t   Telemetry tests read their sink the way any consumer reads a medium —\n9\t   cursor at `:dao.stream/oldest`, then `next` until it blocks — over the\n10\t   unbounded memory log, so an assertion sees every datom a run emitted\n11\t   rather than the tail a ring buffer happened to keep.\n12\t\n13\t   Stream-driven tests thread an observer session — a medium the test owns, a\n14\t   unary attacher bound to it, an attached observer, and a consumer — which\n15\t   is the composition the REPL uses, at test scale. The semantic VM's\n16\t   composition has two such stages over two media\n17\t   (`make-encoder-session`). The VM holds no program stream of its own.\"\n18\t  (:require [dao.stream :as stream]\n19\t            [dao.stream.memory-log :as memory-log]\n20\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ringbuffer]\n21\t            [dao.stream.observer :as observer]\n22\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n23\t            [yin.vm.ast-walker :as ast-walker]\n24\t            [yin.vm.encoder :as encoder]\n25\t            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n26\t            [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as linearize]\n27\t            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]))\n28\t\n29\t\n30\t(def default-capacity 64)\n31\t\n32\t\n33\t(def secret\n34\t  \"The capability secret these test compositions give a task\n35\t   (yin.vm.linker.md section 7.3, r10): injected and deterministic, so\n36\t   every host runs the same seals. A test of cross-task forgery composes\n37\t   its tasks with distinct secrets.\"\n38\t  \"yin.vm.test-utils/capability-secret\")\n39\t\n40\t\n41\t(defn make-stream\n42\t  \"A `:make-stream` over the v2 ring buffer. A nil capacity is the VM's\n43\t   default, not an unbounded stream: v2 has no unbounded mode.\"\n44\t  [capacity]\n45\t  (ringbuffer/create! {:dao.stream/type ringbuffer/transport-type,"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"e4cf725d-0850-423c-8892-7eef368374c8","timestamp":"2026-11-18T16:21:02.163Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-fixorder/test/yin/vm/test_utils.cljc","content":"(ns yin.vm.test-utils\n  \"Composition helpers for the v2 VM suite.\n\n   Every v2 test supplies `:make-stream`: the VM has no default transport, so\n   a test that omits it gets a VM that cannot create streams. The ring buffer\n   is the composition's choice here, not the VM's.\n\n   Telemetry tests read their sink the way any consumer reads a medium —\n   cursor at `:dao.stream/oldest`, then `next` until it blocks — over the\n   unbounded memory log, so an assertion sees every datom a run emitted\n   rather than the tail a ring buffer happened to keep.\n\n   Stream-driven tests thread an observer session — a medium the test owns, a\n   unary attacher bound to it, an attached observer, and a consumer — which\n   is the composition the REPL uses, at test scale. The semantic VM's\n   composition has two such stages over two media\n   (`make-encoder-session`). The VM holds no program stream of its own.\"\n  (:require [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.memory-log :as memory-log]\n            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ringbuffer]\n            [dao.stream.observer :as observer]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.ast-walker :as ast-walker]\n            [yin.vm.encoder :as encoder]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as linearize]\n            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]))\n\n\n(def default-capacity 64)\n\n\n(def secret\n  \"The capability secret these test compositions give a task\n   (yin.vm.linker.md section 7.3, r10): injected and deterministic, so\n   every host runs the same seals. A test of cross-task forgery composes\n   its tasks with distinct secrets.\"\n  \"yin.vm.test-utils/capability-secret\")\n\n\n(defn make-stream\n  \"A `:make-stream` over the v2 ring buffer. A nil capacity is the VM's\n   default, not an unbounded stream: v2 has no unbounded mode.\"\n  [capacity]\n  (ringbuffer/create! {:dao.stream/type ringbuffer/transport-type,","numLines":45,"startLine":1,"totalLines":217}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"call_c5bedbc1343b4109ac701251","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
