{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_07c81870813d4e14aad0c4b1","type":"tool_result","content":"2960\t;; `read-forms` is the frontend's parser — the reader itself — and\n2961\t;; `lower-unit` lowers what it reads to the entry's argument: one thunk\n2962\t;; whose call runs the program compiled under the argument-vector\n2963\t;; convention and the outcome model over the guest library, with every\n2964\t;; top-level definition published to the runtime global namespace\n2965\t;; (`clj/define-global!`/`clj/global-get`), as a Python def lands in\n2966\t;; its module's globals. No call node is rewritten and no foreign\n2967\t;; `:code` is extracted: the unit is the program's own lowering,\n2968\t;; wrapped.\n2969\t\n2970\t(def unit-opts\n2971\t  \"The `compile-program` opts a linked unit compiles with: the\n2972\t   argument-vector convention with the outcome model over the guest\n2973\t   library's adapters. The required clj module supplies the continuation\n2974\t   family; VM primitives are callable directly by bare name.\"\n2975\t  {:convention :arg-vector,\n2976\t   :outcomes true,\n2977\t   :linked-runtime true,\n2978\t   :adapters library-adapters,\n2979\t   :native vm/primitive-profiles})\n2980\t\n2981\t\n2982\t(def top-defining-operators\n2983\t  \"The operators whose second element names a top-level definition.\"\n2984\t  '#{def defn defn- defmacro})\n2985\t\n2986\t\n2987\t(defn read-forms\n2988\t  \"Every form `source` text reads. The reader is the parser: a malformed\n2989\t   source throws, as any frontend's refused parse does.\n2990\t\n2991\t   Source-string compilation is a JVM/Node capability (tools.reader is\n2992\t   an mvn dependency, absent from the jolt host's source-root classpath\n2993\t   — the jolt lane loads compiled output and ships source strings to\n2994\t   remote evaluators, so this is unreachable there; the honest error\n2995\t   says so if ever reached).\"\n2996\t  [source]\n2997\t  #?(:cljd (throw (ex-info \"Source-string compilation requires the JVM/Node reader; ClojureDart compiles from forms\"\n2998\t                           {:yang.clojure/reader :unavailable-on-cljd}))\n2999\t     :jolt (throw (ex-info \"Source-string compilation requires the JVM/Node reader; the jolt host compiles from forms or delegates source reading to its remote evaluators\"\n3000\t                           {:yang.clojure/reader :unavailable-on-jolt}))\n3001\t     :default\n3002\t     (let [rd (rt/string-push-back-reader source)]\n3003\t       (loop [forms []]\n3004\t         (let [form (treader/read rd false ::eof)]\n3005\t           (if (= form ::eof)\n3006\t             forms\n3007\t             (recur (conj forms form))))))))\n3008\t\n3009\t\n3010\t(defn top-level-names\n3011\t  \"The names `forms` define at the top level, in order: the second element\n3012\t   of each def/defn/defn-/defmacro head.\"\n3013\t  [forms]\n3014\t  (into []\n3015\t        (comp (filter #(and (seq? %) (contains? top-defining-operators (first %))))\n3016\t              (map (comp strip-symbol-meta second)))\n3017\t        forms))\n3018\t\n3019\t\n3020\t(declare publish-to-globals)\n3021\t\n3022\t\n3023\t(defn- globals-child\n3024\t  [x names bound]\n3025\t  (cond\n3026\t    (and (map? x) (contains? x :type)) (publish-to-globals x names bound)\n3027\t    (vector? x) (mapv #(globals-child % names bound) x)\n3028\t    :else x))\n3029\t\n3030\t\n3031\t(defn- publish-to-globals\n3032\t  \"Rewrite the compiled `node` for the linked unit: a top-level\n3033\t   definition in `names` becomes a `clj/define-global!` write and a free\n3034\t   read of one becomes a `clj/global-get`, both under the name's string.\n3035\t   The `names` a unit is lowered with are its own top-level definitions,\n3036\t   its guest library's and the projected names the composition bound in\n3037\t   the runtime global namespace, so a projected export and a definition\n3038\t   read through the one binding: a definition the unit itself runs\n3039\t   publishes after the projection and shadows it. A store definition\n3040\t   inside the unit thunk is conditional to the linker, so no body read\n3041\t   of it discharges (the runtime preludes avoid this by keeping every\n3042\t   definition at module level); the runtime global namespace is the\n3043\t   linked unit's definition table instead, as a Python module body\n3044\t   writes its dictionary. Lexically bound names, quoted literals and\n3045\t   macro definitions keep their store shape: a macro is not a runtime\n3046\t   value.\"\n3047\t  [node names bound]\n3048\t  (case (:type node)\n3049\t    :literal node\n3050\t    :vm/current-continuation node\n3051\t    :variable (if (and (contains? names (:name node))\n3052\t                       (not (contains? bound (:name node))))\n3053\t                (u/app (u/v 'clj/global-get) (u/lit (str (:name node))))\n3054\t                node)\n3055\t    :lambda (assoc node :body (publish-to-globals (:body node) names\n3056\t                                                  (into bound (:params node))))\n3057\t    :application\n3058\t    (if (and (= 'yin/def (get-in node [:operator :name]))\n3059\t             (= 2 (count (:operands node)))\n3060\t             (= :literal (:type (first (:operands node))))\n3061\t             (contains? names (:value (first (:operands node)))))\n3062\t      (u/app (u/v 'clj/define-global!)\n3063\t             (u/lit (str (:value (first (:operands node)))))\n3064\t             (publish-to-globals (second (:operands node)) names bound))\n3065\t      (assoc node\n3066\t             :operator (publish-to-globals (:operator node) names bound)\n3067\t             :operands (mapv #(publish-to-globals % names bound)\n3068\t                             (:operands node))))\n3069\t    :if (cond-> node\n3070\t          (contains? node :test)\n3071\t          (assoc :test (publish-to-globals (:test node) names bound))\n3072\t          (contains? node :consequent)\n3073\t          (assoc :consequent (publish-to-globals (:consequent node) names bound))\n3074\t          (contains? node :alternate)\n3075\t          (assoc :alternate (publish-to-globals (:alternate node) names bound)))\n3076\t    (reduce (fn [n k]\n3077\t              (let [v (get n k)]\n3078\t                (if (or (and (map? v) (contains? v :type)) (vector? v))\n3079\t                  (assoc n k (globals-child v names bound))\n3080\t                  n)))\n3081\t            node (keys node))))\n3082\t\n3083\t\n3084\t(defn lower-unit\n3085\t  \"The `clj/run-main` entry's unit for the top-level source `forms`: one\n3086\t   thunk whose call runs the program — `forms` plus the definitions of\n3087\t   the guest library they need, compiled unmodified under `unit-opts`\n3088\t   and published to the runtime global namespace by\n3089\t   `publish-to-globals` — so the helper's export projection can read\n3090\t   each top-level definition. The two-argument form also takes the\n3091\t   projected `exports` (names the composition already bound in the\n3092\t   runtime global namespace): their free reads publish the same way, so\n3093\t   the projection is the caller's binding for them. The program's own\n3094\t   `yang.call` call sites need no free-name declaration: the convention\n3095\t   preamble `compile-program` emits defines those names locally, and\n3096\t   the donor publication pins the `yang.call` module for the qualified\n3097\t   reads that remain.\"\n3098\t  ([forms] (lower-unit forms []))\n3099\t  ([forms exports]\n3100\t   (let [source (vec forms)\n3101\t         library (library-for source)\n3102\t         program (compile-program (concat source library) true unit-opts)\n3103\t         macros (into #{}\n3104\t                      (comp (filter #(and (seq? %) (= 'defmacro (first %))))\n3105\t                            (map (comp strip-symbol-meta second)))\n3106\t                      (concat source library))\n3107\t         names (reduce disj\n3108\t                       (into (set (top-level-names source))\n3109\t                             (concat (map (comp strip-symbol-meta second) library)\n3110\t                                     (map symbol exports)))\n3111\t                       macros)]\n3112\t     ;; `publish-to-globals` rewrites nodes after `compile-program`\n3113\t     ;; finalized them, so the unit is finalized again over its\n3114\t     ;; finished tree: the rewrite's own applications are occurrences.\n3115\t     (annotate-call-sites (u/lam [] (publish-to-globals program names #{}))))))\n3116\t\n3117\t\n3118\t(defn output\n3119\t  \"The `clj/run-main` value as test data.\"\n3120\t  [value]\n3121\t  (pr-str value))\n3122\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"1109a37e-9f76-47e7-ab21-a18e6f8f6e08","timestamp":"2026-11-18T16:21:53.823Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-fixorder/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc","content":";; `read-forms` is the frontend's parser — the reader itself — and\n;; `lower-unit` lowers what it reads to the entry's argument: one thunk\n;; whose call runs the program compiled under the argument-vector\n;; convention and the outcome model over the guest library, with every\n;; top-level definition published to the runtime global namespace\n;; (`clj/define-global!`/`clj/global-get`), as a Python def lands in\n;; its module's globals. No call node is rewritten and no foreign\n;; `:code` is extracted: the unit is the program's own lowering,\n;; wrapped.\n\n(def unit-opts\n  \"The `compile-program` opts a linked unit compiles with: the\n   argument-vector convention with the outcome model over the guest\n   library's adapters. The required clj module supplies the continuation\n   family; VM primitives are callable directly by bare name.\"\n  {:convention :arg-vector,\n   :outcomes true,\n   :linked-runtime true,\n   :adapters library-adapters,\n   :native vm/primitive-profiles})\n\n\n(def top-defining-operators\n  \"The operators whose second element names a top-level definition.\"\n  '#{def defn defn- defmacro})\n\n\n(defn read-forms\n  \"Every form `source` text reads. The reader is the parser: a malformed\n   source throws, as any frontend's refused parse does.\n\n   Source-string compilation is a JVM/Node capability (tools.reader is\n   an mvn dependency, absent from the jolt host's source-root classpath\n   — the jolt lane loads compiled output and ships source strings to\n   remote evaluators, so this is unreachable there; the honest error\n   says so if ever reached).\"\n  [source]\n  #?(:cljd (throw (ex-info \"Source-string compilation requires the JVM/Node reader; ClojureDart compiles from forms\"\n                           {:yang.clojure/reader :unavailable-on-cljd}))\n     :jolt (throw (ex-info \"Source-string compilation requires the JVM/Node reader; the jolt host compiles from forms or delegates source reading to its remote evaluators\"\n                           {:yang.clojure/reader :unavailable-on-jolt}))\n     :default\n     (let [rd (rt/string-push-back-reader source)]\n       (loop [forms []]\n         (let [form (treader/read rd false ::eof)]\n           (if (= form ::eof)\n             forms\n             (recur (conj forms form))))))))\n\n\n(defn top-level-names\n  \"The names `forms` define at the top level, in order: the second element\n   of each def/defn/defn-/defmacro head.\"\n  [forms]\n  (into []\n        (comp (filter #(and (seq? %) (contains? top-defining-operators (first %))))\n              (map (comp strip-symbol-meta second)))\n        forms))\n\n\n(declare publish-to-globals)\n\n\n(defn- globals-child\n  [x names bound]\n  (cond\n    (and (map? x) (contains? x :type)) (publish-to-globals x names bound)\n    (vector? x) (mapv #(globals-child % names bound) x)\n    :else x))\n\n\n(defn- publish-to-globals\n  \"Rewrite the compiled `node` for the linked unit: a top-level\n   definition in `names` becomes a `clj/define-global!` write and a free\n   read of one becomes a `clj/global-get`, both under the name's string.\n   The `names` a unit is lowered with are its own top-level definitions,\n   its guest library's and the projected names the composition bound in\n   the runtime global namespace, so a projected export and a definition\n   read through the one binding: a definition the unit itself runs\n   publishes after the projection and shadows it. A store definition\n   inside the unit thunk is conditional to the linker, so no body read\n   of it discharges (the runtime preludes avoid this by keeping every\n   definition at module level); the runtime global namespace is the\n   linked unit's definition table instead, as a Python module body\n   writes its dictionary. Lexically bound names, quoted literals and\n   macro definitions keep their store shape: a macro is not a runtime\n   value.\"\n  [node names bound]\n  (case (:type node)\n    :literal node\n    :vm/current-continuation node\n    :variable (if (and (contains? names (:name node))\n                       (not (contains? bound (:name node))))\n                (u/app (u/v 'clj/global-get) (u/lit (str (:name node))))\n                node)\n    :lambda (assoc node :body (publish-to-globals (:body node) names\n                                                  (into bound (:params node))))\n    :application\n    (if (and (= 'yin/def (get-in node [:operator :name]))\n             (= 2 (count (:operands node)))\n             (= :literal (:type (first (:operands node))))\n             (contains? names (:value (first (:operands node)))))\n      (u/app (u/v 'clj/define-global!)\n             (u/lit (str (:value (first (:operands node)))))\n             (publish-to-globals (second (:operands node)) names bound))\n      (assoc node\n             :operator (publish-to-globals (:operator node) names bound)\n             :operands (mapv #(publish-to-globals % names bound)\n                             (:operands node))))\n    :if (cond-> node\n          (contains? node :test)\n          (assoc :test (publish-to-globals (:test node) names bound))\n          (contains? node :consequent)\n          (assoc :consequent (publish-to-globals (:consequent node) names bound))\n          (contains? node :alternate)\n          (assoc :alternate (publish-to-globals (:alternate node) names bound)))\n    (reduce (fn [n k]\n              (let [v (get n k)]\n                (if (or (and (map? v) (contains? v :type)) (vector? v))\n                  (assoc n k (globals-child v names bound))\n                  n)))\n            node (keys node))))\n\n\n(defn lower-unit\n  \"The `clj/run-main` entry's unit for the top-level source `forms`: one\n   thunk whose call runs the program — `forms` plus the definitions of\n   the guest library they need, compiled unmodified under `unit-opts`\n   and published to the runtime global namespace by\n   `publish-to-globals` — so the helper's export projection can read\n   each top-level definition. The two-argument form also takes the\n   projected `exports` (names the composition already bound in the\n   runtime global namespace): their free reads publish the same way, so\n   the projection is the caller's binding for them. The program's own\n   `yang.call` call sites need no free-name declaration: the convention\n   preamble `compile-program` emits defines those names locally, and\n   the donor publication pins the `yang.call` module for the qualified\n   reads that remain.\"\n  ([forms] (lower-unit forms []))\n  ([forms exports]\n   (let [source (vec forms)\n         library (library-for source)\n         program (compile-program (concat source library) true unit-opts)\n         macros (into #{}\n                      (comp (filter #(and (seq? %) (= 'defmacro (first %))))\n                            (map (comp strip-symbol-meta second)))\n                      (concat source library))\n         names (reduce disj\n                       (into (set (top-level-names source))\n                             (concat (map (comp strip-symbol-meta second) library)\n                                     (map symbol exports)))\n                       macros)]\n     ;; `publish-to-globals` rewrites nodes after `compile-program`\n     ;; finalized them, so the unit is finalized again over its\n     ;; finished tree: the rewrite's own applications are occurrences.\n     (annotate-call-sites (u/lam [] (publish-to-globals program names #{}))))))\n\n\n(defn output\n  \"The `clj/run-main` value as test data.\"\n  [value]\n  (pr-str value))\n","numLines":163,"startLine":2960,"totalLines":3122}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"call_07c81870813d4e14aad0c4b1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
