{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20261119002343c049a859f6fb4d1f","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"`run-session` uses `load-fresh-program` = `vm/fresh-code-loader ast-walker/vm-load-program vm/ast-contract` — the AST-walker's datom loader. `queue-rows!` would queue rows as the program batch, but `ast-walker/vm-load-program` expects datoms... hmm, there's also `vm-load-rows` (line 934 in ast_walker.cljc). So a rows session would use a rows loader. For executing row sets, the semantic lane in call_test: `load-semantic-ast` = `vm/fresh-code-loader semantic/load-ast vm/ast-contract` and then `(vm/run (load-semantic-ast (semantic/create-vm opts)) (vm/ast->datoms ast))` — wait, that passes DATOMS to semantic/load-ast. Hmm: `semantic/load-ast` loads map-AST. For my legacy fixture I have rows — `semantic/load-vector` after `linearize/project-rows`? In run-encoder-session: rows → (linearize/project-rows rows) → semantic/load-vector machine. And replay-snapshot uses `linearize/project-rows tree nil rows` — projecting a tree + frontend metadata to a semantic vector.\n\nSo the legacy-load route: fixture row-set {:root r :rows {...}} → `linearize/project-rows` → `semantic/load-vector` → run. Let me check the semantic lane runner more closely in call_test: `:semantic (fn [ast] (vm/run (load-semantic-ast (semantic/create-vm opts) (vm/ast->datoms ast))))` — passes ast as datoms? `vm/ast->datoms` converts AST → datoms; semantic/load-ast loads a datom batch into the semantic VM. OK.\n\nFor rows: is there a loader that takes the row set directly? `vm-load-rows` in ast_walker (line 934). Let me look at it — the walker can load row sets directly. That's the cleanest legacy execution route: walker lane over rows.","signature":"e62c21a4ccbb4ad1854304b0"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-4