{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20261119002352de070b0c1e3f4a06","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"`ast-walker/vm-load-rows` is the direct route to load a row-set fixture and execute. It runs `vm/semantic-bytecode->ast` validation. So the family-7 legacy test: read the pre-fix fixture EDN (rows + root), `vm-load-rows` into a walker VM, `vm/run`, `vm/value`. \n\nNow — capture the pre-fix fixture NOW (before any fix). Design:\n\nFixture program P (native): `((fn [x] {(+ x 1) :a (- x 1) :b}) 1)`.\n- Pre-fix JVM order: form built by test → array-map, insertion order (+ x 1), (- x 1). Emitted operands: {} (+ x 1) :a (- x 1) :b. Execution: assoc {} 2 :a 2 :b → {2 :b}.\n- Post-fix: canonical order — which pair is later? Determined by address bytes. Let me actually COMPUTE the roots right now in a REPL-ish test so the fixture and expectations are grounded, and confirm old vs new winner differs. If both orders give the same winner (i.e., canonical order happens to equal insertion order), pick swapped insertion or different value mapping so they differ (making the legacy-execution assertion meaningful). I'll compute pre-fix: compile, project operand roots, sort → determine new order.\n\nI also want the arity-map fixture for family 1's \"ordered child-address vector\" recorded expectation. That needs post-fix recording (mandated red first though — the ORDER assertion uses the ruled order [fn, reason, argc] which I can determine pre-fix by computing child roots myself... the ruling already TELLS us the order: fn, reason, argc. But better to compute independently in-test via the expectation builder, then ALSO assert equals the ruling's stated order [[:yin.k/fn] [:yin.vm.data/reason] [:yin.k/argc]] as a literal recorded expectation).\n\nLet me now write a scratch diagnostic test namespace to compute the key roots and orders pre-fix (RED evidence), then design tests. Actually — more efficient: write the actual new test namespace now (families 1-7), using independent expectation builders everywhere, run it pre-fix to confirm RED, then implement, then re-run to green. For recorded digests (family 1's child-address vector), record post-fix.\n\nOne more thing to understand: `expand-like-the-repl` and the macro lane. Let me read it.","signature":"e5b624ab24d448999ea1b56d"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"11e22eff-b4b2-4ce1-8f5c-73773581769b","timestamp":"2026-11-18T16:24:03.456Z","thinking_duration_ms":9299,"thinking_display":"updates"}
