{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_3fade36dc7d7426b9b0d810c","type":"tool_result","content":"350\t(defn- expand-like-the-repl\n351\t  \"Expand compiled `ast` through the REPL pipeline's production stages:\n352\t   `encoder/program-batch` (what `yin.repl`'s eval-program appends to\n353\t   program-in) into the row-native expander, seeded as the REPL seeds\n354\t   its session expander — the standard forms folded through a throwaway\n355\t   context, then a fresh session context holding that store. Answers\n356\t   `{:ctx ctx :result expansion}`, where `ctx` is the admitting\n357\t   context (its `:t` is the batch's source coordinate).\"\n358\t  [ast]\n359\t  (let [store (macro/seed-store\n360\t                (macro/make-ctx {:token :callsite-test/standard-forms\n361\t                                 :source-medium :callsite-test/standard-forms})\n362\t                [macro/stdlib-forms])\n363\t        ctx (macro/make-ctx {:token \"callsite-test\"\n364\t                             :source-medium :program-in\n365\t                             :store store})]\n366\t    {:ctx ctx\n367\t     :result (macro/expand-batch (encoder/program-batch ast) ctx)}))\n368\t\n369\t\n370\t(deftest post-expansion-coverage-test\n371\t  (testing \"the marker set covers the tree the REPL pipeline actually executes\"\n372\t    (let [ast (yang/compile-program\n373\t                '[(defmacro unless\n374\t                    [c a b]\n375\t                    (yin/if c b a))\n376\t                  (unless false (+ 1 2) 0)])\n377\t          {:keys [ctx result]} (expand-like-the-repl ast)\n378\t          {:keys [status tree frontend-metadata log]} result\n379\t          ;; the row set the evaluator loaders consume from program-out\n380\t          final (macro/packet->row-set tree)\n381\t          ;; the ADMISSION origin of this expansion — the table's key\n382\t          ;; coordinate, never a blanket stamp on the rows (design §2.1:\n383\t          ;; generated post-expansion syntax must not be mislabeled as\n384\t          ;; original source)\n385\t          admission [:source :program-in (:t ctx) 0]\n386\t          input-tree (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)\n387\t          input-tables (vm/ast-side-tables ast input-tree admission)\n388\t          ;; the expansion record addresses the log actually holds: the\n389\t          ;; only legitimate `[:expansion a]` origins are these\n390\t          event-addrs (into #{} (map first) (nth log 1))\n391\t          origins (row-origins frontend-metadata)]\n392\t      (is (= :ok status))\n393\t      (testing \"expansion changed the tree: the `(unless …)` call expanded\"\n394\t        (is (not= (:root input-tree) (:root final))))\n395\t      (testing \"the changed root carries no fabricated expansion origin\n396\t                (design §2.1: post-expansion names the pipeline\n397\t                boundary, not proof that a generating event occurred)\"\n398\t        (is (seq frontend-metadata))\n399\t        (is (every? (fn [o]\n400\t                      (or (= o admission)\n401\t                          (and (expansion-origin? o)\n402\t                               (contains? event-addrs (second o)))))\n403\t                    origins)\n404\t            \"every origin is the admission's source origin or names a\n405\t             recorded expansion event — nothing fabricated\")\n406\t        ;; the `(unless …)` output's generated node is an `:if`, not an\n407\t        ;; application, and its `(+ 1 2)` operand is the admitted\n408\t        ;; operand passed through — so every APPLICATION here is\n409\t        ;; retained admitted syntax and genuinely keeps the source\n410\t        ;; origin; the source origin is not a blanket stamp, it is the\n411\t        ;; real provenance of each marked occurrence\n412\t        (is (= #{admission} origins)\n413\t            \"no generating event produced an application here, so every\n414\t             marked occurrence is admitted\"))"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"98452eab-766d-42ef-bed5-255f70274bb9","timestamp":"2026-11-18T16:24:03.841Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-fixorder/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc","content":"(defn- expand-like-the-repl\n  \"Expand compiled `ast` through the REPL pipeline's production stages:\n   `encoder/program-batch` (what `yin.repl`'s eval-program appends to\n   program-in) into the row-native expander, seeded as the REPL seeds\n   its session expander — the standard forms folded through a throwaway\n   context, then a fresh session context holding that store. Answers\n   `{:ctx ctx :result expansion}`, where `ctx` is the admitting\n   context (its `:t` is the batch's source coordinate).\"\n  [ast]\n  (let [store (macro/seed-store\n                (macro/make-ctx {:token :callsite-test/standard-forms\n                                 :source-medium :callsite-test/standard-forms})\n                [macro/stdlib-forms])\n        ctx (macro/make-ctx {:token \"callsite-test\"\n                             :source-medium :program-in\n                             :store store})]\n    {:ctx ctx\n     :result (macro/expand-batch (encoder/program-batch ast) ctx)}))\n\n\n(deftest post-expansion-coverage-test\n  (testing \"the marker set covers the tree the REPL pipeline actually executes\"\n    (let [ast (yang/compile-program\n                '[(defmacro unless\n                    [c a b]\n                    (yin/if c b a))\n                  (unless false (+ 1 2) 0)])\n          {:keys [ctx result]} (expand-like-the-repl ast)\n          {:keys [status tree frontend-metadata log]} result\n          ;; the row set the evaluator loaders consume from program-out\n          final (macro/packet->row-set tree)\n          ;; the ADMISSION origin of this expansion — the table's key\n          ;; coordinate, never a blanket stamp on the rows (design §2.1:\n          ;; generated post-expansion syntax must not be mislabeled as\n          ;; original source)\n          admission [:source :program-in (:t ctx) 0]\n          input-tree (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)\n          input-tables (vm/ast-side-tables ast input-tree admission)\n          ;; the expansion record addresses the log actually holds: the\n          ;; only legitimate `[:expansion a]` origins are these\n          event-addrs (into #{} (map first) (nth log 1))\n          origins (row-origins frontend-metadata)]\n      (is (= :ok status))\n      (testing \"expansion changed the tree: the `(unless …)` call expanded\"\n        (is (not= (:root input-tree) (:root final))))\n      (testing \"the changed root carries no fabricated expansion origin\n                (design §2.1: post-expansion names the pipeline\n                boundary, not proof that a generating event occurred)\"\n        (is (seq frontend-metadata))\n        (is (every? (fn [o]\n                      (or (= o admission)\n                          (and (expansion-origin? o)\n                               (contains? event-addrs (second o)))))\n                    origins)\n            \"every origin is the admission's source origin or names a\n             recorded expansion event — nothing fabricated\")\n        ;; the `(unless …)` output's generated node is an `:if`, not an\n        ;; application, and its `(+ 1 2)` operand is the admitted\n        ;; operand passed through — so every APPLICATION here is\n        ;; retained admitted syntax and genuinely keeps the source\n        ;; origin; the source origin is not a blanket stamp, it is the\n        ;; real provenance of each marked occurrence\n        (is (= #{admission} origins)\n            \"no generating event produced an application here, so every\n             marked occurrence is admitted\"))","numLines":65,"startLine":350,"totalLines":3098}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"call_3fade36dc7d7426b9b0d810c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
