{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202611190025005d62ac797a04411f","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The plain (non-outcome) av lane: `av-opts {:convention :arg-vector :native (set (keys vm/primitives))}` and `av-modules` = default registry + stream + cell + data. Under non-outcome convention, the arity else branch is `(data/count dsg__av)` which the data module refuses with :reason :arity — the payload is the data module's refusal, not the arity-error map. The arity-error map (with :yin.k/fn etc.) only appears with `:outcomes true`. The outcome runner (`run-outcome`) uses outcome-modules = av-modules + 'portable host module with outcome-adapted nth + 'probe. And `outcome-opts {:convention :arg-vector, :outcomes true, :native (set (keys vm/primitives)), :adapters {'data/nth 'portable/nth}}`.\n\nWait — but the cohort's unit-opts uses `:adapters library-adapters` and `:native vm/primitive-profiles`. For MY payload-values test I can use a local copy of outcome-opts/outcome-modules (modeled on clojure_test's, portable). Does `run-outcome` work on all hosts? It's in clojure_test.clj (JVM-only) but uses only portable pieces (tu/, yang/outcome-adapter, vm/primitive-profile, module/register-host-module). The callsite test runs on all 4 hosts — does IT use register-host-module anywhere... The r2 report says the callsite battery runs 40 tests on Node/Dart. I'll model my namespace's requires on the callsite test's (which is proven portable on all four hosts): requires clojure.test, dao.jing, yang.clojure, yang.clojure.prelude?, yang.core.call?, yin.vm, yin.vm.encoder, yin.vm.module, yin.vm.data, yin.vm.macro, yin.vm.semantic.linearize, yin.vm.semantic.derive, yin.vm.test-utils?, dao.jing.mem, yin.vm.linker.publish...\n\nWait — is `yin.vm.test-utils` portable to Dart/Jolt? It requires dao.stream, dao.stream.memory-log, dao.stream.ringbuffer, dao.stream.observer — cljc files. Are they in the cljd aggregation (bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj --only)? The Dart lane compiles the namespace + deps. dao.stream.ringbuffer on Dart — dart datagram quirks memory suggests dao.stream works on Dart. The callsite test itself requires `#?@(:clj [[dao.stream :as stream] [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ring]])` — gated to :clj! So dao.stream IS problematic on non-JVM hosts?? But test-utils requires it ungated... and clojure_test.clj is JVM-only anyway. Hmm — do any PORTABLE (4-host) tests require yin.vm.test-utils? yang.core.call-test — is IT in the J2 included list? No (not listed). Does call_test run on Dart? Let me check cljd_agg to see how namespaces are selected and whether test-utils is Dart-clean.","signature":"93169effb67a4e4998a244e0"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"51f76b76-407e-4792-b3c6-0944d15f3315","timestamp":"2026-11-18T16:25:09.950Z","thinking_duration_ms":8736,"thinking_display":"updates"}
