{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_1a726615c62e4d02b3a4c9c4","type":"tool_result","content":"(ns cljd-agg\n  \"Dart test runner that aggregates the generated test files.\n\n   `flutter test` loads every generated *_test.dart separately (about 7.5 s\n   each). This runner compiles the test namespaces through the cljd tool,\n   groups the generated files into a few shard files that import them and call\n   each `main`, and runs `flutter test` on the shards only. Shards live under\n   build/, never under test/, so a plain `cljd test` never runs them twice.\n\n   Run with babashka:\n     bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj [--slow-only | --slow-regex | --only NS,NS...]\n   --slow-only restricts the run to the namespaces that use dao.test-slow/guard.\n   A namespace in that set with no generated Dart file is fatal.\n   --only compiles and runs only the given test namespaces (bb test:changed,\n   bb test:sub); one with no generated Dart file is fatal too, EXCEPT a\n   JVM-only namespace: one whose every deftest sits behind a reader\n   conditional that excludes ClojureDart (for example\n   dao.data.sorted-user-type-test). The cljd tool compiles such a namespace as\n   a plain library (lib/cljd-out/<ns>.dart exists) and emits no test file;\n   that is reported and skipped, never fatal. A namespace that produced\n   neither file is still fatal.\n   --slow-regex prints, for bb.edn, an anchored alternation of those\n   namespaces with its dots already escaped for embedding in an EDN string\n   (shadow-cljs --config-merge); it is not a ready-to-use regex. It exits 1\n   when no namespace uses the guard, so a slow lane cannot be vacuous.\n   DATOM_SLOW_TESTS is inherited from the environment.\"\n  (:require\n    [babashka.fs :as fs]\n    [babashka.process :as p]\n    [clojure.string :as str]))\n\n\n(def test-root \"test\")\n(def out-root \"test/cljd-out\")\n(def shard-dir \"build/cljd-agg\")\n(def max-shards 8)\n\n\n(defn- ns-of\n  \"The namespace declared by the first ns form of `file`.\"\n  [file]\n  (second (re-find #\"\\(ns\\s+\\^?(?:\\{[^}]*\\}\\s+)?([^\\s\\)]+)\" (slurp file))))\n\n\n(defn- source-files\n  []\n  (->> (file-seq (fs/file test-root))\n       (filter #(re-find #\"_test\\.clj[cd]$\" (str %)))\n       (remove #(str/includes? (str %) \"cljd-out\"))\n       (map str)\n       sort))\n\n\n(defn- test-namespaces\n  \"Distinct: a namespace with both a .cljc and a .cljd source (for example\n   dao.stream.cbor-test) has one generated Dart file, which must run once.\"\n  []\n  (distinct (keep ns-of (source-files))))","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"76a72f16-b2eb-44b4-b89d-6b84c6ebae69","timestamp":"2026-11-18T16:25:10.182Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"(ns cljd-agg\n  \"Dart test runner that aggregates the generated test files.\n\n   `flutter test` loads every generated *_test.dart separately (about 7.5 s\n   each). This runner compiles the test namespaces through the cljd tool,\n   groups the generated files into a few shard files that import them and call\n   each `main`, and runs `flutter test` on the shards only. Shards live under\n   build/, never under test/, so a plain `cljd test` never runs them twice.\n\n   Run with babashka:\n     bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj [--slow-only | --slow-regex | --only NS,NS...]\n   --slow-only restricts the run to the namespaces that use dao.test-slow/guard.\n   A namespace in that set with no generated Dart file is fatal.\n   --only compiles and runs only the given test namespaces (bb test:changed,\n   bb test:sub); one with no generated Dart file is fatal too, EXCEPT a\n   JVM-only namespace: one whose every deftest sits behind a reader\n   conditional that excludes ClojureDart (for example\n   dao.data.sorted-user-type-test). The cljd tool compiles such a namespace as\n   a plain library (lib/cljd-out/<ns>.dart exists) and emits no test file;\n   that is reported and skipped, never fatal. A namespace that produced\n   neither file is still fatal.\n   --slow-regex prints, for bb.edn, an anchored alternation of those\n   namespaces with its dots already escaped for embedding in an EDN string\n   (shadow-cljs --config-merge); it is not a ready-to-use regex. It exits 1\n   when no namespace uses the guard, so a slow lane cannot be vacuous.\n   DATOM_SLOW_TESTS is inherited from the environment.\"\n  (:require\n    [babashka.fs :as fs]\n    [babashka.process :as p]\n    [clojure.string :as str]))\n\n\n(def test-root \"test\")\n(def out-root \"test/cljd-out\")\n(def shard-dir \"build/cljd-agg\")\n(def max-shards 8)\n\n\n(defn- ns-of\n  \"The namespace declared by the first ns form of `file`.\"\n  [file]\n  (second (re-find #\"\\(ns\\s+\\^?(?:\\{[^}]*\\}\\s+)?([^\\s\\)]+)\" (slurp file))))\n\n\n(defn- source-files\n  []\n  (->> (file-seq (fs/file test-root))\n       (filter #(re-find #\"_test\\.clj[cd]$\" (str %)))\n       (remove #(str/includes? (str %) \"cljd-out\"))\n       (map str)\n       sort))\n\n\n(defn- test-namespaces\n  \"Distinct: a namespace with both a .cljc and a .cljd source (for example\n   dao.stream.cbor-test) has one generated Dart file, which must run once.\"\n  []\n  (distinct (keep ns-of (source-files))))","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"call_1a726615c62e4d02b3a4c9c4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"subcommandResults"}}]}
