{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20261119002923078016cd20ca4843","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wait — my `ctors` walk is wrong: `walk/postwalk #(if (coll? %) % [%])` wraps collections in vectors, producing garbage. Let me use a simpler tree-walk: the AST is nested maps/vectors. Use `tree-seq` with branch? Maps and vectors both seq-able... Simplest correct: walk/postwalk identity and collect nodes matching predicate:\n\n```clojure\n(defn- collect-ctors [ast]\n  (let [acc (atom [])]\n    (walk/postwalk (fn [n] (when (and (map? n) (ctor? n)) (swap! acc conj n)) n) ast)\n    @acc))\n```\n\npostwalk visits every nested map/vector element. That works — nodes are maps; children reachable via vals. Let me rewrite the file properly.","signature":"d867712eb35643ea9ce71def"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"2c928582-7335-438d-98ac-1f20f05bc417","timestamp":"2026-11-18T16:29:29.966Z","thinking_duration_ms":2900,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20261119002923078016cd20ca4843","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_6839eddcf08d4cfda7f99c7a","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 -c 'from pathlib import Path\nPath(\"test/fixorder_tmp_diag_test.cljc\").write_text(\"\"\"(ns fixorder-tmp-diag-test\n  \\\"Scratch diagnostics: compute canonical orders from pre-fix child rows.\\\"\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is]]\n            [clojure.walk :as walk]\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [yang.clojure :as yang]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]))\n\n(def forms-av\n  (quote [(defn replay\n            [x]\n            (let [[a b] [x 1.5]]\n              (+ (identity ^:replay a) (identity ^:replay a) b)))\n          (replay 2)]))\n\n(defn- ctor?\n  [n]\n  (and (map? n)\n       (= :application (:type n))\n       (= :variable (get-in n [:operator :type]))\n       (contains? #{(quote assoc) (quote conj)} (get-in n [:operator :name]))\n       (= :literal (get-in n [:operands 0 :type]))\n       (contains? #{{} [] #{}} (get-in n [:operands 0 :value]))))\n\n(defn- collect\n  [ast]\n  (let [acc (atom [])]\n    (walk/postwalk (fn [n] (when (ctor? n) (swap! acc conj n)) n) ast)\n    @acc))\n\n(deftest diag-test\n  (let [ast (yang/compile-program forms-av true yang/unit-opts)\n        ctors (collect ast)]\n    (println :ctors (count ctors))\n    (doseq [c ctors\n            :when (= (quote assoc) (get-in c [:operator :name]))]\n      (let [ops (:operands c)\n            roots (mapv (fn [o] (:root (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode o))) ops)\n            lits (mapv (fn [o] (when (= :literal (:type o)) (pr-str (:value o)))) ops)]\n        (println :ctor)\n        (println :lits lits)\n        (println :roots roots))))\n  (let [form (quote ((fn [x] {(+ x 1) :a (- x 1) :b}) 1))\n        ast (yang/compile form)\n        ctors (collect ast)]\n    (println :collision-ctors (count ctors))\n    (doseq [c ctors]\n      (let [ops (:operands c)\n            roots (mapv (fn [o] (:root (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode o))) ops)]\n        (println :lits (mapv (fn [o] (when (= :literal (:type o)) (pr-str (:value o)))) ops))\n        (println :roots roots)\n        (println :sorted?\n                 (mapv (fn [[a b]] (jing/canonical-compare a b))\n                       (partition 2 1 roots)))))))\n\"\"\")'","description":"Rewrite scratch diagnostic correctly"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"4f36cf1e-0658-4222-a41f-89a824b33db5","timestamp":"2026-11-18T16:29:34.972Z","wire_tool_inputs":{"call_6839eddcf08d4cfda7f99c7a":{"command":"python3 -c 'from pathlib import Path\nPath(\"test/fixorder_tmp_diag_test.cljc\").write_text(\"\"\"(ns fixorder-tmp-diag-test\n  \\\"Scratch diagnostics: compute canonical orders from pre-fix child rows.\\\"\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is]]\n            [clojure.walk :as walk]\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [yang.clojure :as yang]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]))\n\n(def forms-av\n  (quote [(defn replay\n            [x]\n            (let [[a b] [x 1.5]]\n              (+ (identity ^:replay a) (identity ^:replay a) b)))\n          (replay 2)]))\n\n(defn- ctor?\n  [n]\n  (and (map? n)\n       (= :application (:type n))\n       (= :variable (get-in n [:operator :type]))\n       (contains? #{(quote assoc) (quote conj)} (get-in n [:operator :name]))\n       (= :literal (get-in n [:operands 0 :type]))\n       (contains? #{{} [] #{}} (get-in n [:operands 0 :value]))))\n\n(defn- collect\n  [ast]\n  (let [acc (atom [])]\n    (walk/postwalk (fn [n] (when (ctor? n) (swap! acc conj n)) n) ast)\n    @acc))\n\n(deftest diag-test\n  (let [ast (yang/compile-program forms-av true yang/unit-opts)\n        ctors (collect ast)]\n    (println :ctors (count ctors))\n    (doseq [c ctors\n            :when (= (quote assoc) (get-in c [:operator :name]))]\n      (let [ops (:operands c)\n            roots (mapv (fn [o] (:root (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode o))) ops)\n            lits (mapv (fn [o] (when (= :literal (:type o)) (pr-str (:value o)))) ops)]\n        (println :ctor)\n        (println :lits lits)\n        (println :roots roots))))\n  (let [form (quote ((fn [x] {(+ x 1) :a (- x 1) :b}) 1))\n        ast (yang/compile form)\n        ctors (collect ast)]\n    (println :collision-ctors (count ctors))\n    (doseq [c ctors]\n      (let [ops (:operands c)\n            roots (mapv (fn [o] (:root (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode o))) ops)]\n        (println :lits (mapv (fn [o] (when (= :literal (:type o)) (pr-str (:value o)))) ops))\n        (println :roots roots)\n        (println :sorted?\n                 (mapv (fn [[a b]] (jing/canonical-compare a b))\n                       (partition 2 1 roots)))))))\n\"\"\")'","description":"Rewrite scratch diagnostic correctly"}}}
