{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_ead3cdfad2664f009fb88356","type":"tool_result","content":"1255\t\n1256\t\n1257\t(defn decode-snapshot\n1258\t  \"The value of one accepted Jing payload (byte[], Uint8Array or\n1259\t   Uint8List) that already passed ingress: bytes a backend stored after\n1260\t   `decode` accepted them, or bytes this codec encoded itself. Refuses\n1261\t   malformed CBOR, trailing data and anything outside the closed profile,\n1262\t   but does not re-encode the value to prove canonicality -- that check\n1263\t   ran once at ingress (docs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md, Layering and\n1264\t   interfaces). Returned byte strings are fresh copies.\"\n1265\t  [bs]\n1266\t  (when (zero? (bytes/length bs))\n1267\t    (refuse :malformed-cbor \"empty input\"))\n1268\t  (let [[item pos] (read-item bs 0 1)]\n1269\t    (when (not= pos (bytes/length bs))\n1270\t      (refuse :trailing-data (str (- (bytes/length bs) pos) \" bytes after the item\")))\n1271\t    (item->value bs item)))\n1272\t\n1273\t\n1274\t(defn decode\n1275\t  \"The value of one canonical Jing payload (byte[], Uint8Array or\n1276\t   Uint8List): the ingress check. Refuses everything `decode-snapshot`\n1277\t   refuses and also any payload whose value does not re-encode to exactly\n1278\t   these bytes. Returned byte strings are fresh copies.\"\n1279\t  [bs]\n1280\t  (let [value (decode-snapshot bs)]\n1281\t    (when-not (bytes= bs (encode value))\n1282\t      (refuse :non-canonical))\n1283\t    value))\n1284\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"2c715eb3-b958-402e-830e-251ac4d437c1","timestamp":"2026-11-18T16:32:53.915Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-fixorder/src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc","content":"\n\n(defn decode-snapshot\n  \"The value of one accepted Jing payload (byte[], Uint8Array or\n   Uint8List) that already passed ingress: bytes a backend stored after\n   `decode` accepted them, or bytes this codec encoded itself. Refuses\n   malformed CBOR, trailing data and anything outside the closed profile,\n   but does not re-encode the value to prove canonicality -- that check\n   ran once at ingress (docs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md, Layering and\n   interfaces). Returned byte strings are fresh copies.\"\n  [bs]\n  (when (zero? (bytes/length bs))\n    (refuse :malformed-cbor \"empty input\"))\n  (let [[item pos] (read-item bs 0 1)]\n    (when (not= pos (bytes/length bs))\n      (refuse :trailing-data (str (- (bytes/length bs) pos) \" bytes after the item\")))\n    (item->value bs item)))\n\n\n(defn decode\n  \"The value of one canonical Jing payload (byte[], Uint8Array or\n   Uint8List): the ingress check. Refuses everything `decode-snapshot`\n   refuses and also any payload whose value does not re-encode to exactly\n   these bytes. Returned byte strings are fresh copies.\"\n  [bs]\n  (let [value (decode-snapshot bs)]\n    (when-not (bytes= bs (encode value))\n      (refuse :non-canonical))\n    value))\n","numLines":30,"startLine":1255,"totalLines":1284}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"call_ead3cdfad2664f009fb88356","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
