{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_1c673b3515724ce2bd7341d2","type":"tool_result","content":"1087\t(defn create-vm\n1088\t  \"Create a new ASTWalkerVM.\n1089\t\n1090\t   Options:\n1091\t     :env           initial lexical environment\n1092\t     :primitives    primitive operations map\n1093\t     :primitive-profiles published primitive profile registry\n1094\t     :primitive-canonical-names name -> canonical name for intentional aliases\n1095\t     :modules       module registry value (see `yin.vm.module`)\n1096\t     :make-stream   (fn [capacity] -> create outcome); no default\n1097\t     :call-in       explicit inbound request handle\n1098\t     :call-out      explicit outbound response handle\n1099\t     :call-out-cursor, :ffi-caller-id  `yin.vm/empty-state`'s\n1100\t     :call-capacity capacity for a constructed FFI pair\n1101\t     :bridge        host FFI handlers\n1102\t\n1103\t   There is no `:in-stream`: program observation belongs to\n1104\t   `dao.stream.observer`, and an obsolete `:in-stream` option is\n1105\t   rejected here, before any FFI resource is allocated.\n1106\t\n1107\t   Construction is all-or-nothing: creating the FFI pair and minting the\n1108\t   call-out cursor are stream operations, and any non-`ok` outcome fails here\n1109\t   rather than leaving a half-built VM. The bridge cursor is minted by\n1110\t   `ffi/attach` below; the program cursor belongs to observer attachment.\"\n1111\t  ([] (create-vm {}))\n1112\t  ([opts]\n1113\t   (when (contains? opts :in-stream)\n1114\t     (throw (ex-info\n1115\t              \"Program observation moved to dao.stream.observer: a VM no longer accepts :in-stream\"\n1116\t              {:in-stream (:in-stream opts)})))\n1117\t   (let [env (vm/check-bindings! :env (or (:env opts) {}))\n1118\t         base (vm/empty-state\n1119\t                (assoc (select-keys opts\n1120\t                                    [:primitives :primitive-profiles\n1121\t                                     :primitive-canonical-names :modules\n1122\t                                     :make-stream :call-in :call-out\n1123\t                                     :call-out-cursor :ffi-caller-id\n1124\t                                     :call-capacity :link-request\n1125\t                                     :link-response :origin :ancestry\n1126\t                                     :capability-secret :secret-source\n1127\t                                     :attach-stream :gc-threshold])\n1128\t                       :telemetry (:telemetry opts)\n1129\t                       :vm-model :ast-walker))]\n1130\t     (-> (map->ASTWalkerVM (merge base\n1131\t                                  {:bridge nil,"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"9f16f8ab-36b0-4d80-94f7-18d5d0d7631c","timestamp":"2026-11-18T16:33:06.065Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-fixorder/src/cljc/yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc","content":"(defn create-vm\n  \"Create a new ASTWalkerVM.\n\n   Options:\n     :env           initial lexical environment\n     :primitives    primitive operations map\n     :primitive-profiles published primitive profile registry\n     :primitive-canonical-names name -> canonical name for intentional aliases\n     :modules       module registry value (see `yin.vm.module`)\n     :make-stream   (fn [capacity] -> create outcome); no default\n     :call-in       explicit inbound request handle\n     :call-out      explicit outbound response handle\n     :call-out-cursor, :ffi-caller-id  `yin.vm/empty-state`'s\n     :call-capacity capacity for a constructed FFI pair\n     :bridge        host FFI handlers\n\n   There is no `:in-stream`: program observation belongs to\n   `dao.stream.observer`, and an obsolete `:in-stream` option is\n   rejected here, before any FFI resource is allocated.\n\n   Construction is all-or-nothing: creating the FFI pair and minting the\n   call-out cursor are stream operations, and any non-`ok` outcome fails here\n   rather than leaving a half-built VM. The bridge cursor is minted by\n   `ffi/attach` below; the program cursor belongs to observer attachment.\"\n  ([] (create-vm {}))\n  ([opts]\n   (when (contains? opts :in-stream)\n     (throw (ex-info\n              \"Program observation moved to dao.stream.observer: a VM no longer accepts :in-stream\"\n              {:in-stream (:in-stream opts)})))\n   (let [env (vm/check-bindings! :env (or (:env opts) {}))\n         base (vm/empty-state\n                (assoc (select-keys opts\n                                    [:primitives :primitive-profiles\n                                     :primitive-canonical-names :modules\n                                     :make-stream :call-in :call-out\n                                     :call-out-cursor :ffi-caller-id\n                                     :call-capacity :link-request\n                                     :link-response :origin :ancestry\n                                     :capability-secret :secret-source\n                                     :attach-stream :gc-threshold])\n                       :telemetry (:telemetry opts)\n                       :vm-model :ast-walker))]\n     (-> (map->ASTWalkerVM (merge base\n                                  {:bridge nil,","numLines":45,"startLine":1087,"totalLines":1275}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"call_1c673b3515724ce2bd7341d2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
