en compiled under different env? env affects symbols: free symbols compile as :variable regardless; unit-opts env has ::convention — a free symbol `n`... native-name? checks convention native set — `n` isn't native → compile-variable. Same result. But `(tap :k1)` — `tap` not native → ordinary application ✓.)\n  For lower-unit: the form must be a top-level program: `[(list 'def 'm M)]`? lower-unit publishes globals — `def m {…}` — the map compiles inside. ✓\n- macro expansion: defmacro whose expansion BUILDS a constructed map — e.g. defmacro `pairs->map` that returns `(assoc {} ~@...)`? RULING: macro-generated form maps re-enter compile-form through this same emitter. Test: a macro returning a map FORM constructed at expansion: \n  ```\n  (defmacro build-map [k v] {(quote k) v})  ; hmm macro body builds host map\n  ```\n  A defmacro body that constructs a host map `{k v}` → macro's fn at expansion time builds the map form → expansion output is a map literal with dynamic content → compiled via emitter → canonical order. Then expand-like-the-repl: status :ok, expansion origins not fabricated (every origin is admission or recorded event), tree contains canonically-ordered constructor. The cohort keeps the production twin-call fixture — my namespace adds this focused one.\n\n**Family 7 (legacy):**\n- Load CBOR fixture (pre-fix artifact) → rows; assert recorded old root; `vm-load-rows` + run on walker lane (and semantic lane?) → value = recorded old result {2 :a}; recompile same source now → different root (order changed) and new result {2 :b}; old artifact untouched (its rows still validate: `vm/semantic-bytecode->ast` runs inside load).\n- Keep unannotated legacy-load/missing-C1 refusals — they live in the callsite battery (untouched; I'll note in findings).\n- two different tokens → different origins/keys: compile+project same content with tokens \"token-a\"/\"token-b\" → roots equal, origin sets differ (mirror cohort negative member assertion).\n\n**Family 1 (arity maps):** as analyzed:\n- argument-vector + lower-unit members with cohort source; find named arity map constructor (operand literals contain :yin.k/fn); assert:\n  - literal key order [:yin.k/fn :yin.vm.data/reason :yin.k/argc] — the ruled order;\n  - operand-root vector = recorded vector [201f235c…, 1e03667e…, 3156a070…, 81b62c1e…, 1db5dbd0…, 8930bf5e…, e60543d2…];\n  - pair-keys sorted (oracle);\n  - same for BOTH members;\n  - anonymous arity map (from `[(fn [x] x)]` under unit-opts): key order [:yin.k/kind :yin.k/source :yin.vm.data/reason :yin.k/argc]? From roots: kind 476c5dac, source 58a8f530, reason 81b62c1e, argc 8930bf5e → sorted: 47.. < 58.. < 81.. < 89.. → [kind, source, reason, argc] ✓ (record literals);\n  - anonymous-with-source same order with its own source value;\n  - payload values: `:yin.k/fn 'replay`, reason :arity, argc = (data/count dsg__av) application — assert shapes;\n  - runtime payload values: hmm — \"verify the resulting arity payload values\". Execute: the OUTCOME lane. I'll add a local outcome runner (portable? uses yang/outcome-adapter — cljc ✓, module/register-host-module ✓, data/data-profiles? clojure_test uses `(get data/data-profiles 'nth)` — exists in yin.vm.data? it used `(get data/data-module 'nth)` and `(get data/data-profiles 'nth)` — let me confirm those vars exist (clojure_test requires yin.vm.data as data ✓ same ns). And run via walker only (tu session) — the payload check doesn't need all four lanes (it's about VALUES). Assert `(run-outcome-arity forms)` returns `[:yin.k/error {:yin.vm.data/reason :arity :yin.k/argc N :yin.k/fn 'replay}]`-ish map. Let me check what an arity error outcome looks like — the else branch `(arity-error-form fn-name source)` wrapped in clj/throw → outcome [:yin.k/error raised-map]. The raised value = the constructed map (as data): {:yin.k/fn replay :yin.vm.data/reason :arity :yin.k/argc 2}. RUNTIME result order-independent (it's a map value) — but asserting VALUES verifies semantics preserved. To also verify ORDER at runtime I'd need map iteration — no; values suffice per ruling.\n  - four-host agreement: the recorded digests (family 1d) — I'll include recorded root+keys+c1+provenance digests for the two members in MY namespace (recorded post-fix from JVM).\n\nHmm wait — actually, for family 1's whole-tree digests: these EXACT digests will also be in the re-pinned cohort expectations (same members). Duplication is fine (ruling asks family 1 to assert it; the cohort is the regression gate).\n\nThat's a LOT. Let me also double check `vm/ast->datoms` exists for the semantic runner (call_test uses it ✓).\n\nAlso `linearize/project` for stack/register runners — call_test uses `sr-linearize/project ast` (map AST → semantic vector). ✓\n\nAlso — do stack/register lanes need the cell module? registry = empty + cell + data. call_test uses that for yang.call programs. Mine uses assoc/conj/+ — primitives + data module not even needed... but register/stack machines might need cell for closures? call_test runs closures fine with that registry. Keep it.\n\nOne more check — `vm/primitive-profiles` for create-vm `:primitive-profiles`? call_test's opts don't pass it (only :primitives vm/primitives). OK.\n\nNow, before writing the big namespace — the ENV-var question for run-everywhere with env: `(tu/create-vm (merge opts {:env {'n 1 'tap f}}))` — for stack/register: create-vm opts assoc. Merge env into opts.\n\nNow — the arity-map finder within compile-program(unit-opts): multiple assoc constructors exist (yang.call maps with :yang.call/reason keys). Finder: filter constructors whose operand literals include `(quote :yin.k/fn)` (named) or `:yin.k/kind` (anonymous).\n\nFor the ANONYMOUS arity test: compile `[(with-meta '(fn [x] x) {:line 7 :column 2})]` — wait, under unit-opts a top-level fn form — compile-program compiles it as a plain expression (not called) — av-dispatch still built with arity error else-branch. ✓ From diag: yes, arity map present with 4 pairs even uncalled.\n\nHmm — one thing to check: in the diag, anon map shows :yin.k/source {:line 46 :column 39} for the no-meta variant — READER-position from my diag file. For MY final test, the fn form written in the test file will carry ITS file position — recorded expectation can't hardcode {:line 46...}. So: build the anon no-source form with STRIPPED meta? `(with-meta '(fn [x] x) nil)`? Hmm — reading `'(fn [x] x)` from file gives it meta with file positions. To control: construct `(with-meta (quote (fn [x] x)) nil)`? with-meta nil — meta must be a map or nil — `(with-meta x nil)` works (removes meta? yes, sets meta to nil). But then the INNER forms still carry reader meta — does arity-error-form read `(source-meta form)` of the FN form only — nil meta → no :yin.k/source key → map has 3 pairs [kind, reason, argc]. For the with-source variant use explicit {:line 7 :column 2}. Recorded expectations: for the nil-meta variant, key order [:yin.k/kind :yin.vm.data/reason :yin.k/argc] (roots: kind 476c5dac, reason 81b62c1e, argc 8930bf5e → sorted [47, 81, 89] = kind, reason, argc ✓).\n\nNow — WAIT, one more critical check. The arity-error-form builds the map via `cond->`/`assoc` — a HOST map built at COMPILE time. Its iteration order (host) feeds the emitter. With my fix, the emitter sorts — deterministic. But there's a subtlety: `cond->` assoc order builds an array-map on JVM with ≤8 entries: {:yin.vm.data/reason :arity, :yin.k/argc ..., :yin.k/fn ..., :yin.k/kind ..., :yin.k/source ...} — insertion order fixed. Post-fix irrelevant. ✓\n\nAnother subtlety — `compile-av-fn` may build maps with MORE structure — fine.\n\nNow the LEGACY fixture capture. Also the RECORDING of digests. Order of work (TDD):\n\n1. Write capture namespace for the legacy pre-fix fixture (runs NOW at pre-fix compiler) → writes CBOR + prints old root/value. **Must run BEFORE implementing the fix.**\n2. Write the full test namespace with all expectations except the post-fix recorded digests (family 1d/recorded child-address vector — those are fix-invariant! I already HAVE them from the diagnostics: the operand-root vector post-fix = [201f235c, 1e03667e, 3156a070, 81b62c1e, 1db5dbd0, 8930bf5e, e60543d2] — recorded NOW, valid post-fix). The whole-tree digests for members — need post-fix recording (placeholder markers, filled after implementation).\n3. Run new namespace → RED (order tests fail; permutation tests fail).\n4. Implement emitter + manifest.\n5. Run → mostly green; record whole-tree digests; fill in; re-run green.\n6. Callsite cohort: post-fix digests differ → update replay-expectations + snapshots resource (archive old under pre-fix name); run JVM/Node/Dart gates.\n7. Focused additions to clojure_callsite_test.cljc (family coverage for cohort-adjacent assertions): the ruling says \"add focused regression assertions and replace active expectations only through the controlled re-pin\". I'll add a focused deftest asserting the arity-map constructor order + a comment documenting re-pin.\n8. J2 manifest additions; run Jolt lane (expected refusal — record).\n9. kondo on touched files; ledger; findings.\n\nThe legacy fixture capture — write it now. Contents:\n- program form P = `((fn [x] {(- x 1) :b (+ x 1) :a}) 1)` (old JVM insertion order (- x 1) first).\n- rows = (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode (yang/compile P)) → {:root :rows}.\n- env execution result: run with env {'1...} wait — `(fn [x] ...)` applied to 1 — x bound by lambda. Runner: walker (vm/eval) with primitives assoc. Value = {2 :a} pre-fix.\n- also record `:entry-map` the OLD operand-root vector for the constructor (evidence of old order) and expected post-fix difference.\n\nCBOR encode of {:root kw :rows {kw [...]}} — jing/canonical-bytes (cbor/encode). Write to test/resources/yang/clojure/cc-collection-order-legacy-prefix.cbor. Hmm — name per ruling: \"Versioned post-fix captures/expectations and historical copies needed to retain pre-fix evidence\" — fixture name like `constructed-collection-order-legacy-c1-1.cbo