{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202611190039364eb807d37a7543f7","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Part 3: the corpus definitions and the family-2/3 permutation tests, family-4 oracle test. Note — I need to double check `(trace-of ...)`: my implementation runs values ONCE but resets log after... bug: I capture `values` (running with tap already in env — log fills), then `(do (reset! log []) values)` — the reset happens AFTER the run, so the returned log is EMPTY. Fix: reset log BEFORE run-on:\n\n```clojure\n(defn- trace-of [form env]\n  (let [log (atom [])\n        env (assoc env 'tap (fn [x] (swap! log conj x) x))\n        _ (reset! log [])\n        values (run-on (yang/compile form) env)]\n    (into {} (map (fn [[lane value]] [lane {:value value :log @log}])) values)))\n```\nBut run-on runs all four lanes sequentially over the SAME log — the log accumulates across lanes (4 runs!). Each lane re-executes the program → log would have 4× entries. Fix: run one lane at a time, resetting the log per lane:\n\n```clojure\n(defn- trace-of [form env]\n  (let [ast (yang/compile form)]\n    (into {}\n          (map (fn [lane]\n                 (reset! trace-log [])\n                 [lane {:value ... :log @trace-log}]))\n          ...)))\n```\nrun-on doesn't support per-lane hooks. Restructure: make a lower-level `run-lane [lane ast env]` and have run-on map over it; trace-of resets the log before each lane. Let me rewrite part 2's run-on/trace-of block with an edit. I'll do that when finalizing; note it now.\n\nAlso `(set (vec elements))` — `set` of forms — distinct forms → kept. On cljd `set` exists ✓.\n\nAlso in `trace-of`, the env fn — on the walker, env values host fns — apply works (operator-kind :host-fn). For stack/register lanes: closures/primitives work; env-supplied host fn... the debruijn machines resolve variables to env values and apply — should work like primitives (they're host fns in the registry). Fine.\n\nNow part 3 — corpus + family tests 2,3,4.","signature":"afdfadcfb9c64d92aed44f6a"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"f576dff0-36d1-4b18-a920-68ad23df0211","timestamp":"2026-11-18T16:39:53.813Z","thinking_duration_ms":12245,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202611190039364eb807d37a7543f7","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_89046b3a97534d1988a212c6","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nsrc = r'''\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; RULING 3 test 2: map representation/permutation property\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private quoted-pair-key\n  \"A quoted collection key, one plain and one carrying semantic (non\n   position) metadata inside the literal payload.\"\n  (list 'quote [1 2]))\n\n(def ^:private quoted-meta-key\n  (list 'quote (with-meta [1 2] {:sem true})))\n\n(def ^:private map-corpus\n  \"The recorded corpus of distinct source-entry pairs. Every case holds at\n   least one dynamic expression, so each reaches the emitter as a\n   constructed collection.\"\n  [[:constant-keys-dynamic-values\n    [[:a (list '+ 'n 0)] [:b (list '+ 'n 1)]]]\n   [:dynamic-keys\n    [[(list 'first 'xs) :v1] [(list 'first (list 'rest 'xs)) :v2]]]\n   [:heterogeneous-keys\n    [[:kw (list '+ 'n 0)] [\"str\" 1] [3 1.5] ['sym 2]\n     [quoted-pair-key 3] [quoted-meta-key 4] [true 5] [nil 6]]]\n   [:nested-collections\n    [[:inner-map {:inner (list '+ 'n 1)}]\n     [:inner-set #{(list '+ 'n 2) 3}]\n     [:inner-vec [(list '+ 'n 3)]]\n     [:deep {:a #{[(list '+ 'n 4)]}}]]]\n   [:floats\n    [[1.5 (list '+ 'n 1.5)] [2.25 -0.5] [0.0 2.5]]]\n   [:duplicate-subtrees\n    [[:a (list 'first 'xs)] [:b (list 'first 'xs)] [:c (list 'first 'xs)]]]\n   [:same-key-different-values\n    [[(list '+ 'n 1) :left] [(list '+ 'n 1) :right]]]])\n\n(def ^:private map-corpus-sizes\n  \"Sizes crossing the array-map/hash-map representation thresholds; each\n   gets the full recorded permutation set under both representations.\"\n  [8 9 16 32])\n\n(deftest map-permutation-invariance-test\n  (testing \"sizes 0-4: every insertion permutation, both representations\"\n    (doseq [n (range 5)\n            :let [entries (sized-map-entries n)]]\n      (testing (str \"size \" n)\n        (let [variants (into []\n                             (mapcat (fn [p]\n                                       (for [rep [:array-map :hash-map]]\n                                         (build-map rep (permute entries p)))))\n                             (all-permutations n))\n               snaps (mapv compile-snapshot variants)]\n          (is (pos? (count variants)))\n          (is (apply = snaps)\n              (str n \"-entry permutations diverge: \"\n                   (pr-str (distinct snaps))))\n          (doseq [form variants\n                  :let [ctors (map-constructors (yang/compile form))]]\n            (is (= 1 (count ctors)))\n            (is (ascending? (pair-keys (first ctors)))))))))\n  (testing \"recorded corpus: permutations of the recorded entries\"\n    (doseq [[label entries] map-corpus]\n      (testing (str label)\n        (let [variants (into []\n                             (mapcat (fn [p]\n                                       (for [rep [:array-map :hash-map]]\n                                         (build-map rep (permute entries p)))))\n                             (all-permutations (count entries)))\n               snaps (mapv compile-snapshot variants)]\n          (is (apply = snaps))\n          (doseq [form variants\n                  :let [ctors (map-constructors (yang/compile form))]]\n            (is (ascending? (pair-keys (first ctors)))))))))\n  (testing \"sizes 8/9/16/32: recorded permutations cross the thresholds\"\n    (doseq [n map-corpus-sizes\n            :let [entries (sized-map-entries n)]]\n      (testing (str \"size \" n)\n        (let [variants (into []\n                             (mapcat (fn [p]\n                                       (for [rep [:array-map :hash-map]]\n                                         (build-map rep (permute entries p)))))\n                             (recorded-permutations n 1795017757000))\n               snaps (mapv compile-snapshot variants)]\n          (is (apply = snaps))\n          (doseq [form variants\n                  :let [ctors (map-constructors (yang/compile form))]]\n            (is (ascending? (pair-keys (first ctors)))))))))\n  (testing \"the constant fast path stays a literal\"\n    (is (= {:type :literal :value {:a 1 :b 2}}\n           (yang/compile {:a 1 :b 2})))))\n\n(defn- map-constructors\n  [ast]\n  (into [] (filter #(= (quote assoc) (get-in % [:operator :name])))\n        (collection-applications ast)))\n'''\np = Path(\"test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc\")\np.write_text(p.read_text() + src)\nprint(\"part3 ok\")\nPYEOF","description":"Append part 3 (map corpus + permutation test)"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"ad178258-9d36-4c37-b498-091e9c44ab27","timestamp":"2026-11-18T16:40:05.306Z","wire_tool_inputs":{"call_89046b3a97534d1988a212c6":{"command":"python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nsrc = r'''\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; RULING 3 test 2: map representation/permutation property\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private quoted-pair-key\n  \"A quoted collection key, one plain and one carrying semantic (non\n   position) metadata inside the literal payload.\"\n  (list 'quote [1 2]))\n\n(def ^:private quoted-meta-key\n  (list 'quote (with-meta [1 2] {:sem true})))\n\n(def ^:private map-corpus\n  \"The recorded corpus of distinct source-entry pairs. Every case holds at\n   least one dynamic expression, so each reaches the emitter as a\n   constructed collection.\"\n  [[:constant-keys-dynamic-values\n    [[:a (list '+ 'n 0)] [:b (list '+ 'n 1)]]]\n  