{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202611190040061d53b8327c2e46e2","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Note: `map-constructors` is defined at the END of part 3 but used earlier in the same test — in Clojure, a `defn-` inside the same ns is fine as long as it's defined before RUNTIME use (deftest bodies run after ns load). ✓ (calls resolve at runtime).\n\nWait, one problem: `[:same-key-different-values [[(+ n 1) :left] [(+ n 1) :right]]]` — the two KEYS are IDENTICAL forms `(list '+ 'n 1)` — as host data they're EQUAL → the host map built from them has ONE entry {(+ n 1) :right}! Can't have duplicate keys in a host map. So this corpus case is wrong for MAPS via build-map. The value-root secondary key needs: same COMPILED key content but different host keys — e.g. keys `(+ n 1)` and `(+ n 1)` with different metadata → distinct host values, identical compiled content. So: entries `[[(with-meta (list '+ 'n 1) {:m 1}) :left] [(list '+ 'n 1) :right]]`. Let me fix that corpus entry. Also the \"family 4\" tie case uses the same trick.\n\nAlso `[:inner-map {:inner (list '+ 'n 1)}]` — the VALUE is a map with dynamic content → constructed nested ✓. But careful — `{:inner ...}` built at corpus load; fine.\n\nFix the same-key entry now, and also there's a subtle issue with `all-permutations` — for n=4, `(remove #{i} (range n))` returns a lazy seq — `(into [i] %)` works; I pass `(vec (remove ...))` to the recursion — recursion arg is a vector ✓; mapcat over `(range n)` produces seq of vectors ✓.\n\n`(apply = snaps)` for size-0: variants = 1 permutation × 2 reps = 2 forms — the empty map → constant-form? → literal! Both reps equal {} → compile → literal. compile-snapshot fine (snapshot of literal tree). ctors count 0!! `(is (= 1 (count ctors)))` FAILS for n=0 (and the ascending? over empty pair-keys — `(first ctors)` nil → pair-keys nil → rest of nil → exception!). Fix: guard n=0 case — for size 0 expect ZERO constructors (literal path). Restructure: `(if (zero? n) (is (= [] (map-constructors ...))) (do ...))`. Actually the \"constant fast path\" test covers it; for n=0 skip constructor checks. Let me handle: in the size loop, only run constructor assertions when n>0. Also n=1: map has 1 entry, constant? entries are [k (+ n 0)] — dynamic → constructed ✓ 1 ctor.\n\nAlso `distinct` in failure message — on cljs distinct works ✓.\n\nFix these two issues with a small patch to part 3.","signature":"c7022b4b1d6844bc80824910"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"25b8a7d9-01c9-47ee-b38e-286bcf207dbd","timestamp":"2026-11-18T16:40:18.746Z","thinking_duration_ms":10587,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202611190040061d53b8327c2e46e2","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_9299a927ca7948cca3add3f3","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc\")\nt = p.read_text()\n# fix same-key corpus entry: identical compiled keys must differ as host values (metadata)\nt = t.replace(\"\"\"   [:same-key-different-values\n    [[(list '+ 'n 1) :left] [(list '+ 'n 1) :right]]]])\"\"\",\n\"\"\"   [:same-key-different-values\n    ;; identical key code under different host values (metadata), so both\n    ;; entries survive the host map and the value root breaks the tie\n    [[(with-meta (list '+ 'n 1) {:variant :left}) :left]\n     [(list '+ 'n 1) :right]]]])\"\"\")\n# guard the n=0 literal fast path in the size loop\nt = t.replace(\"\"\"          (doseq [form variants\n                  :let [ctors (map-constructors (yang/compile form))]]\n            (is (= 1 (count ctors)))\n            (is (ascending? (pair-keys (first ctors)))))))))\n  (testing \"recorded corpus\"\"\",\n\"\"\"          (when (pos? n)\n            (doseq [form variants\n                    :let [ctors (map-constructors (yang/compile form))]]\n              (is (= 1 (count ctors)))\n              (is (ascending? (pair-keys (first ctors)))))))))\n  (testing \"recorded corpus\"\"\")\np.write_text(t)\nprint(\"patched\")\nPYEOF","description":"Fix corpus tie entry and empty-map guard"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"9e95b16f-ef01-4b0d-90de-105d82054ae1","timestamp":"2026-11-18T16:40:22.093Z","wire_tool_inputs":{"call_9299a927ca7948cca3add3f3":{"command":"python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc\")\nt = p.read_text()\n# fix same-key corpus entry: identical compiled keys must differ as host values (metadata)\nt = t.replace(\"\"\"   [:same-key-different-values\n    [[(list '+ 'n 1) :left] [(list '+ 'n 1) :right]]]])\"\"\",\n\"\"\"   [:same-key-different-values\n    ;; identical key code under different host values (metadata), so both\n    ;; entries survive the host map and the value root breaks the tie\n    [[(with-meta (list '+ 'n 1) {:variant :left}) :left]\n     [(list '+ 'n 1) :right]]]])\"\"\")\n# guard the n=0 literal fast path in the size loop\nt = t.replace(\"\"\"          (doseq [form variants\n                  :let [ctors (map-constructors (yang/compile form))]]\n            (is (= 1 (count ctors)))\n            (is (ascending? (pair-keys (first ctors)))))))))\n  (testing \"recorded corpus\"\"\",\n\"\"\"          (when (pos? n)\n            (doseq [form variants\n                    :let [ctors (map-constructors (yang/compile form))]]\n              (is (= 1 (count ctors)))\n              (is (ascending? (pair-keys (first ctors)))))))))\n  (testing \"recorded corpus\"\"\")\np.write_text(t)\nprint(\"patched\")\nPYEOF","description":"Fix corpus tie entry and empty-map guard"}}}
