{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_d0386bccf60941fe9e75740f","type":"tool_result","content":"448\t\n449\t(def primitive-profiles\n450\t  \"Portable projection of the standard registry, retained as a convenience.\"\n451\t  (into {} (map (fn [[name entry]]\n452\t                  [name (select-keys entry primitive-profile-keys)]))\n453\t        primitives))\n454\t\n455\t\n456\t(def primitive-canonical-names\n457\t  \"Canonical-name declarations for intentional aliases in `primitives`.\n458\t\n459\t   The table is name -> canonical name, not function -> name, so it remains\n460\t   plain portable data. `=` and `==` intentionally share one host function.\"\n461\t  {'== '=})\n462\t\n463\t\n464\t(defn profile-of\n465\t  \"Return `name`'s published profile from a registry, or nil.\"\n466\t  [registry name]\n467\t  (when-let [entry (get registry name)]\n468\t    (when (and (map? entry) (contains? entry :yin.k/profile))\n469\t      (select-keys entry primitive-profile-keys))))\n470\t\n471\t\n472\t(defn name-of\n473\t  \"Reverse-look up `primitive` by host-object identity.\n474\t\n475\t   Returns nil when unnamed, `::ambiguous` when several names remain after\n476\t   applying `canonical-names`, or the one resolved name. The two-argument\n477\t   form declares no aliases.\"\n478\t  ([primitive-map primitive]\n479\t   (name-of primitive-map {} primitive))\n480\t  ([primitive-map canonical-names primitive]\n481\t   (let [names (->> primitive-map\n482\t                    (keep (fn [[name entry]]\n483\t                            (when (identical? (primitive-function entry)\n484\t                                              primitive)\n485\t                              name)))\n486\t                    (sort-by str)\n487\t                    vec)]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"d5939623-4fbe-499e-9700-3cec499d0e95","timestamp":"2026-11-18T16:42:03.865Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-fixorder/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc","content":"\n(def primitive-profiles\n  \"Portable projection of the standard registry, retained as a convenience.\"\n  (into {} (map (fn [[name entry]]\n                  [name (select-keys entry primitive-profile-keys)]))\n        primitives))\n\n\n(def primitive-canonical-names\n  \"Canonical-name declarations for intentional aliases in `primitives`.\n\n   The table is name -> canonical name, not function -> name, so it remains\n   plain portable data. `=` and `==` intentionally share one host function.\"\n  {'== '=})\n\n\n(defn profile-of\n  \"Return `name`'s published profile from a registry, or nil.\"\n  [registry name]\n  (when-let [entry (get registry name)]\n    (when (and (map? entry) (contains? entry :yin.k/profile))\n      (select-keys entry primitive-profile-keys))))\n\n\n(defn name-of\n  \"Reverse-look up `primitive` by host-object identity.\n\n   Returns nil when unnamed, `::ambiguous` when several names remain after\n   applying `canonical-names`, or the one resolved name. The two-argument\n   form declares no aliases.\"\n  ([primitive-map primitive]\n   (name-of primitive-map {} primitive))\n  ([primitive-map canonical-names primitive]\n   (let [names (->> primitive-map\n                    (keep (fn [[name entry]]\n                            (when (identical? (primitive-function entry)\n                                              primitive)\n                              name)))\n                    (sort-by str)\n                    vec)]","numLines":40,"startLine":448,"totalLines":2202}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"call_d0386bccf60941fe9e75740f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
