{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20261119004237d79103705b744b69","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"There's `clj-prelude/admit` — registers 'kind + 'portable adapter modules over a registry. But the full clj module (clj/try etc.) is a PUBLISHED linker module (module-spec → publish → link), not a simple host module. Executing a full unit-opts program requires the linked runtime — the linker. That's heavy (the callsite cohort's published members do this via publish/publish-module!).\n\nSimpler approach for the payload-value test: use clojure_test's LIGHTER outcome-opts (not unit-opts):\n```clojure\n{:convention :arg-vector :outcomes true :native (set (keys vm/primitives)) :adapters {'data/nth 'portable/nth}}\n```\nwith modules = default + stream + cell + data + 'portable (adapted nth). Under this opts, does an av-fn arity error produce the arity-error map? av-dispatch's else: `(if (outcomes? env) (arity-error-form fn-name source) (list 'data/count))` — outcomes → arity-error-form → `(clj/throw {...})`. clj/throw is... under this env, is 'clj/throw in native? No → guest call → module 'clj op 'throw — NOT registered in outcome-modules! How does clojure_test's outcome lane handle clj/throw then? Let me look at what run-outcome tests throw — `test-outcome-success-and-throw` expects `[:yin.k/error {:yin.k/message \"boom\" ...}]` from `(ex-info ...)`... that's ex-info rewrite, not clj/throw. Let me search clojure_test for clj/throw or arity error outcome tests — maybe the arity error path is tested elsewhere. grep 'arity' in clojure_test.","signature":"ce6465d3098b4e0ba2b09074"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"546747db-e405-44bf-8f71-79b0f82bcc44","timestamp":"2026-11-18T16:42:47.400Z","thinking_duration_ms":4983,"thinking_display":"updates"}
