{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202611190044470d2a1527246043be","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wait — in the colliding test, `(trace-of (inserter es) {'n 1})` — env n=1 → `(- n 1)` = 0, `(- 1 n)` = 0 ✓ collide.\n\nBut CAREFUL: `trace-of` passes env to run-on which runs ALL FOUR lanes — the stack/register lanes need env lookups for free `n` ✓.\n\nHmm, one thing: `(:log ...)` — in trace-of I (will) fix the per-lane log reset. Let me now fix `trace-of` in part 2 (it currently has the empty-log bug and the cross-lane accumulation bug). Rewrite trace-of + run-on to run lane-by-lane:\n\n```clojure\n(defn- run-lane\n  [lane ast env]\n  (let [opts (assoc base-opts :env env)]\n    (case lane\n      :ast-walker (vm/eval (tu/create-vm opts) ast)\n      :semantic (vm/run (load-semantic-ast (semantic/create-vm opts) (vm/ast->datoms ast)))\n      :stack (vm/run (dvm/create-vm (:image (derive/stack-image (:vector (linearize/project ast)))) (assoc opts :contract vm/stack-contract)))\n      :register (vm/run (rvm/create-vm (derive/register-image (:vector (linearize/project ast))) (assoc opts :contract vm/register-contract))))))\n\n(def ^:private lanes [:ast-walker :semantic :stack :register])\n\n(defn- run-on\n  ([ast] (run-on ast {}))\n  ([ast env]\n   (into {} (map (fn [lane] [lane (vm/value (run-lane lane ast env))])) lanes)))\n\n(defn- trace-of [form env]\n  (let [ast (yang/compile form)\n        log (atom [])\n        env (assoc env 'tap (fn [x] (swap! log conj x) x))]\n    (into {} (map (fn [lane]\n                    (reset! log [])\n                    (let [v (vm/value (run-lane lane ast env))]\n                      [lane {:value v :log @log}])))\n          lanes)))\n```\n\nReplace part 2's run-on/trace-of block.","signature":"9a2f944c22214d18804c7b65"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"7c5dbf4a-4faa-4d86-8028-04e8d2548657","timestamp":"2026-11-18T16:44:55.788Z","thinking_duration_ms":5169,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202611190044470d2a1527246043be","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_eaf51c2272b44d19926338d9","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc\")\nt = p.read_text()\nA = \"(defn- run-on\"\nB = \";; =============================================================================\\n;; Deterministic permutation machinery\"\ni, j = t.find(A), t.find(B)\nassert i != -1 and j != -1 and i < j\nnew = r'''(def ^:private lanes\n  \"The four execution routes the behavior tests run.\"\n  [:ast-walker :semantic :stack :register])\n\n(defn- run-lane\n  \"Run compiled `ast` on one execution route.\"\n  [lane ast env]\n  (let [opts (assoc base-opts :env env)]\n    (case lane\n      :ast-walker (vm/eval (tu/create-vm opts) ast)\n      :semantic (vm/run (load-semantic-ast (semantic/create-vm opts)\n                                           (vm/ast->datoms ast)))\n      :stack (vm/run (dvm/create-vm\n                       (:image (derive/stack-image\n                                 (:vector (linearize/project ast))))\n                       (assoc opts :contract vm/stack-contract)))\n      :register (vm/run (rvm/create-vm\n                          (derive/register-image\n                            (:vector (linearize/project ast)))\n                          (assoc opts :contract vm/register-contract))))))\n\n(defn- run-on\n  \"Run compiled `ast` on every execution route with `env`, returning\n   lane -> value.\"\n  ([ast] (run-on ast {}))\n  ([ast env]\n   (into {} (map (fn [lane] [lane (vm/value (run-lane lane ast env))]))\n         lanes)))\n\n(defn- run-form\n  \"Compile and run `form` on every route with `env`.\"\n  ([form] (run-form form {}))\n  ([form env] (run-on (yang/compile form) env)))\n\n(defn- trace-of\n  \"The observable evaluation of `form` on every route: the lane@s value\n   together with the ordered log the env-bound `tap` host function\n   recorded during THAT lane@s run. `tap` echoes its argument, so a log is\n   exactly the order that lane consumed the operands in.\"\n  [form env]\n  (let [ast (yang/compile form)\n        log (atom [])\n        env (assoc env @tap@ (fn [x] (swap! log conj x) x))]\n    (into {} (map (fn [lane]\n                    (reset! log [])\n                    (let [value (vm/value (run-lane lane ast env))]\n                      [lane {:value value :log @log}])))\n          lanes)))\n\n\n'''.replace(\"@\", chr(39))\nt = t[:i] + new + t[j:]\np.write_text(t)\nprint(\"runners rewritten\")\nPYEOF","description":"Fix trace-of per-lane logging"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"b1d48b1f-89ab-49ae-9a80-c4f31f578b6d","timestamp":"2026-11-18T16:45:00.892Z","wire_tool_inputs":{"call_eaf51c2272b44d19926338d9":{"command":"python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc\")\nt = p.read_text()\nA = \"(defn- run-on\"\nB = \";; =============================================================================\\n;; Deterministic permutation machinery\"\ni, j = t.find(A), t.find(B)\nassert i != -1 and j != -1 and i < j\nnew = r'''(def ^:private lanes\n  \"The four execution routes the behavior tests run.\"\n  [:ast-walker :semantic :stack :register])\n\n(defn- run-lane\n  \"Run compiled `ast` on one execution route.\"\n  [lane ast env]\n  (let [opts (assoc base-opts :env env)]\n    (case lane\n      :ast-walker (vm/eval (tu/create-vm opts) ast)\n      :semantic (vm/run (load-semantic-ast (semantic/create-vm opts)\n                                           (vm/ast->datoms ast)))\n      :stack (vm/run (dvm/create-vm\n                       (:image (derive/stack-image\n                                 (:vector (linearize/project ast))))\n                       (assoc opts :contract vm/stack-contract)))\n      :register (vm/run (rvm/create-vm\n                          (derive/register-image\n                            (:vector (linearize/project ast)))\n                          (assoc opts :contract vm/register-contract))))))\n\n(defn- run-on\n  \"Run compiled `ast` on every execution route with `env`, returning\n   lane -> value.\"\n  ([ast] (run-on ast {}))\n  ([ast env]\n   (into {} (map (fn [lane] [lane (vm/value (run-lane lane ast env))]))\n         lanes)))\n\n(defn- run-form\n  \"Compile and run `form` on every route with `env`.\"\n  ([form] (run-form form {}))\n  ([form env] (run-on (yang/compile form) env)))\n\n(defn- trace-of\n  \"The observable evaluation of `form` on every route: the lane@s value\n   together with the ordered log the env-bound `tap` host function\n   recorded during THAT lane@s run. `tap` echoes its argument, so a log is\n   exactly the order that lane consumed the operands in.\"\n  [form env]\n  (let [ast (yang/compile form)\n        log (atom [])\n        env (assoc env @tap@ (fn [x] (swap! log conj x) x))]\n    (into {} (map (fn [lane]\n                    (reset! log [])\n                    (let [value (vm/value (run-lane lane ast env))]\n                      [lane {:value value :log @log}])))\n          lanes)))\n\n\n'''.replace(\"@\", chr(39))\nt = t[:i] + new + t[j:]\np.write_text(t)\nprint(\"runners rewritten\")\nPYEOF","description":"Fix trace-of per-lane logging"}}}
