{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20261119004521c321ae9ce1ac4ac6","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Hmm, several problems in part 8:\n\n1. The `ctor-roots` binding is dead/broken code — remove.\n2. The `find-map` filter compares `(get-in c [:operands 2 :value])` — nonsense leftover. Remove ctor-roots entirely.\n3. The macro test: `tag-pair` macro — `(defmacro tag-pair [k v] (array-map k v))` — macro body builds a host ARRAY-MAP at expansion time → the expansion output is a map form with dynamic content → hits my emitter when the expanded form compiles? WAIT — NO. Macro expansion happens at the EXPANDER (row-native, post-compile — the macro function executes at expansion over ROWS). The macro's body was COMPILED by yang/compile-program — `(array-map k v)` inside the macro body is an APPLICATION of array-map — not a map literal. The macro RETURNS (at expansion time, as a guest value) a host map — which the expander re-encodes as a form. So the emitter never sees it... Actually — does it? The macro function is a compiled guest fn; `(array-map k v)` is compiled as an av-application of `array-map`... which isn't a primitive → guest call → module 'array-map missing... The macro wouldn't even run!\n\nThe ruling's text: \"Later compiler-generated form maps that re-enter `compile-form` pass through this same emitter.\" Where do compiler-generated FORM MAPS re-enter compile-form? In `compile-program`/av-fn internals: e.g. `arity-error-form` (the map built by cond->) is passed to compile-form via `lower-top-form`/av-dispatch → compile-form-1 → literal? → not constant → constructed-collection ✓ THAT's the compiler-generated map path. Also `compile-av-fn` descriptor maps? For the macro test, simpler: use a macro whose EXPANSION introduces a map literal — e.g. `(defmacro wrap [x] {:tag x})`? The macro BODY `{:tag x}` — a map literal with dynamic x → compiled by the emitter INSIDE the macro's compiled body — the macro fn RETURNS the map value at expansion → the resulting VALUE (a guest map value, not a form)... hmm, the expander treats returned data as forms — a returned MAP VALUE would be re-encoded... as data or as syntax? This gets deep into the expander.\n\nSAFER macro test design: assert that (a) the macro member of the equality gate (the production twin-call fixture) is retained — that's the callsite cohort's job (kept); (b) pre-expansion normalization doesn't fabricate/erase origins — use the EXISTING production macro fixture from the cohort (defmacro twin ... (yin/if ... (yin/application (yin/variable 'f) [(yin/literal 1)]))) — it exercises the real expansion chain without map construction. My namespace: expand that same program, assert status ok + origins unfabricated (mirroring post-expansion-coverage-test) PLUS verify that the input tree's constructed collections (if any) kept C1 coverage: actually the twin fixture has no constructed maps. \n\nLet me simplify the macro test to what the ruling asks: \"Keep the real production macro/twin-call fixture and the complete expansion-record chain in the equality gate. Prove that pre-expansion collection normalization does not fabricate or erase expansion origins.\" → The equality gate = the callsite cohort (unchanged, keeps macro member). In MY namespace: a macro program that CALLS a macro expanding to an expression CONTAINING a constructed map via yin/forms: \n\n```clojure\n[(defmacro mktree [x]\n   (yin/if (yin/literal true)\n     (yin/application (yin/variable 'assoc)\n                      [(yin/literal {}) (yin/variable x) (yin/literal :k)])\n     (yin/literal nil)))\n (mktree q)]\n```\nHmm — that's an EXPLICIT assoc application (not emitter output). To get EMITTER output in a macro expansion, the macro must return a MAP FORM — via yin/map? Is there a yin constructor for maps? Let me check what yin.* forms exist (yin/literal, yin/variable, yin/application, yin/if...). If there's yin/map or similar... Actually simpler: the macro can build the form with HOST code at... no — defmacro bodies are guest code.\n\nAlternative honest approach: the ruling's \"compiler-generated arity maps\" + \"entry points\" already cover generation. For the macro boundary, use the cohort's production twin fixture unchanged and assert the expansion chain + no fabricated origins (the cohort's assertion, duplicated here as the collection-order namespace's guard that normalization didn't disturb expansion). I'll rewrite the macro test to use the twin fixture (copy of the cohort's macro-ast) and assert: status :ok, expansion-log digest recorded?, origins unfabricated, input tree's C1 coverage validates. Plus — the KEY question for THIS round: does the input tree still carry its markers through expansion when it contains a constructed map? I'll include a constructed map in the PROGRAM SOURCE alongside the macro call: `[(defmacro twin [x] ...) (defn replay [x] ...) (replay 2)]`-ish where replay's body contains a dynamic map → the expansion input tree contains emitter output; expansion must retain status ok + origins honest.\n\nLet me rewrite part 8's macro block. Also fix the entry-points block (remove dead code). Let me rewrite the whole part-8 section cleanly: replace from \";; RULING 3 test 6\" header to end of file with a corrected version.","signature":"0c5f68ad462545cf92242104"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"a379c39d-533c-4097-92b9-71095131406c","timestamp":"2026-11-18T16:45:42.969Z","thinking_duration_ms":19903,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20261119004521c321ae9ce1ac4ac6","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_ede50ff1983c497282285a09","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc\")\nt = p.read_text()\nA = \";; =============================================================================\\n;; RULING 3 test 6: entry points and generation\"\ni = t.find(A)\nassert i != -1\nnew = r''';; =============================================================================\n;; RULING 3 test 6: entry points and generation\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private entry-map-form\n  \"One dynamic map whose canonical order the oracle below derives; the\n   written insertion deliberately differs from a sorted reading.\"\n  {(list 'tap' :k2) (list 'tap' :v2)\n   (list 'tap' :k1) (list 'tap' :v1)})\n\n(defn- map-operand-roots\n  \"The ordered child-address vectors of every constructed map of `ast`.\"\n  [ast]\n  (->> (collection-applications ast)\n       (filter (fn [c] (= (quote assoc') (get-in c [:operator :name]))))\n       (mapv child-roots)))\n\n(deftest entry-points-order-test\n  (testing \"compile-form, compile, compile-program (both modes) and\n            lower-unit emit one canonical operand vector\"\n    (let [unit-forms [(list 'def' 'm' entry-map-form)]\n          asts {:compile-form (yang/compile-form entry-map-form)\n                :compile (yang/compile entry-map-form)\n                :compile-program-native (yang/compile-program [entry-map-form])\n                :compile-program-unit (yang/compile-program unit-forms true yang/unit-opts)\n                :lower-unit (yang/lower-unit unit-forms)}\n          reference (map-operand-roots (:compile-form asts))]\n      (is (= 1 (count reference)))\n      (doseq [[entry ast] asts]\n        (testing (str entry)\n          (let [roots (map-operand-roots ast)]\n            (is (pos? (count roots)))\n            (is (apply = roots) \"every constructed map in the entry agrees\")\n            (is (= (vec reference) (vec roots))))))))\n  (testing \"compiler-generated maps (the arity helper) are covered\"\n    (is (ascending?\n          (pair-keys (first (arity-map-constructors\n                              (yang/compile-program cohort-forms\n                                                    true yang/unit-opts))))))))\n\n\n(defn- expand-like-the-repl\n  \"The REPL production expansion stages over compiled `ast` (the callsite\n   battery's helper, local copy).\"\n  [ast]\n  (let [store (macro/seed-store\n                (macro/make-ctx {:token :order-test/standard-forms\n                                 :source-medium :order-test/standard-forms})\n                [macro/stdlib-forms])\n        ctx (macro/make-ctx {:token \"order-test\"\n                             :source-medium :program-in\n                             :store store})]\n    {:ctx ctx\n     :result (macro/expand-batch (encoder/program-batch ast) ctx)}))\n\n(deftest expansion-origins-unfabricated-test\n  \"The real production macro/twin-call fixture (the equality gate keeps its\n   complete expansion-record chain): a program that also contains a\n   constructed map expands cleanly, and pre-expansion collection\n   normalization fabricates no expansion origin and erases none.\"\n  (let [ast (yang/compile-program\n              '[(defmacro twin\n                  [x]\n                  (yin/if (yin/literal true) x\n                          (yin/application (yin/variable 'f) [(yin/literal 1)])))\n                (defn holder\n                  [x]\n                  {:kept (first (list x))})\n                (twin (holder 1))])\n        {:keys [ctx result]} (expand-like-the-repl ast)\n        {:keys [status tree frontend-metadata log]} result\n        admission [:source :program-in (:t ctx) 0]\n        event-addrs (into #{} (map first) (nth log 1))\n        origins (into #{}\n                      (comp (filter (fn [row] (= :yang/call-site (nth row 3))))\n                            (map first))\n                      frontend-metadata)\n        input-tree (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)\n        final (macro/packet->row-set tree)]\n    (is (= :ok status))\n    (is (not= (:root input-tree) (:root final))\n        \"the twin call really expanded\")\n    (is (seq frontend-metadata))\n    (is (every? (fn [o]\n                  (or (= o admission)\n                      (and (vector? o) (= :expansion (first o))\n                           (contains? event-addrs (second o)))))\n                origins)\n        \"every origin is the admission or names a recorded expansion event\")\n    (is (pos? (count (map-operand-roots ast)))\n        \"the program carries a constructed map through expansion\")))\n'''.replace(\"'\", \"@\").replace(\"@\", chr(39))\n# careful: replace \"'\" back is identity; we only need the raw text as-is\nt = t[:i] + new\np.write_text(t)\nprint(\"part8 rewritten\")\nPYEOF","description":"Rewrite family 6 tests cleanly"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"248fe6dc-c020-48a1-ad7c-28cfdd7998cc","timestamp":"2026-11-18T16:45:53.181Z","wire_tool_inputs":{"call_ede50ff1983c497282285a09":{"command":"python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc\")\nt = p.read_text()\nA = \";; =============================================================================\\n;; RULING 3 test 6: entry points and generation\"\ni = t.find(A)\nassert i != -1\nnew = r''';; =============================================================================\n;; RULING 3 test 6: entry points and generation\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private entry-map-form\n  \"One dynamic map whose canonical order the oracle below derives; the\n   written insertion deliberately differs from a sorted reading.\"\n  {(list 'tap' :k2) (list 'tap' :v2)\n   (list 'tap' :k1) (list 'tap' :v1)})\n\n(defn- map-operand-roots\n  \"The ordered child-address vectors of every constructed map of `ast`.\"\n  [ast]\n  (->> (collection-applications ast)\n       (filter (fn [c] (= (quote assoc') (get-in c [:operator :name]))))\n       (mapv child-roots)))\n\n(deftest entry-points-order-test\n  (testing \"compile-form, compile, compile-program (both modes) and\n            lower-unit emit one canonical operand vector\"\n    (let [unit-forms [(list 'def' 'm' entry-map-form)]\n          asts {:compile-form (yang/compile-form entry-map-form)\n                :compile (yang/compile entry-map-form)\n                :compile-program-native (yang/compile-program [entry-map-form])\n                :compile-program-unit (yang/compile-program unit-forms true yang/unit-opts)\n                :lower-unit (yang/lower-unit unit-forms)}\n          reference (map-operand-roots (:compile-form asts))]\n      (is (= 1 (count reference)))\n      (doseq [[entry ast] asts]\n        (testing (str entry)\n          (let [roots (map-operand-roots ast)]\n            (is (pos? (count roots)))\n            (is (apply = roots) \"every constructed map in the entry agrees\")\n            (is (= (vec reference) (vec roots))))))))\n  (testing \"compiler-generated maps (the arity helper) are covered\"\n    (is (ascending?\n          (pair-keys (first (arity-map-constructors\n                              (yang/compile-program cohort-forms\n                                                    true yang/unit-opts))))))))\n\n\n(defn- expand-like-the-repl\n  \"The REPL production expansion stages over compiled `ast` (the callsite\n   battery's helper, local copy).\"\n  [ast]\n  (let [store (macro/seed-store\n                (macro/make-ctx {:token :order-test/standard-forms\n                                 :source-medium :order-test/standard-forms})\n                [macro/stdlib-forms])\n        ctx (macro/make-ctx {:token \"order-test\"\n                             :source-medium :program-in\n                             :store store})]\n    {:ctx ctx\n     :result (macro/expand-batch (encoder/program-batch ast) ctx)}))\n\n(deftest expansion-origins-unfabricated-test\n  \"The real production macro/twin-call fixture (the equality gate keeps its\n   complete expansion-record chain): a program that also contains a\n   constructed map expands cleanly, and pre-expansion collection\n   normalization fabricates no expansion origin and erases none.\"\n  (let [ast (yang/compile-program\n              '[(defmacro twin\n                  [x]\n                  (yin/if (yin/literal true) x\n                          (yin/application (yin/variable 'f) [(yin/literal 1)])))\n                (defn holder\n                  [x]\n                  {:kept (first (list x))})\n                (twin (holder 1))])\n        {:keys [ctx result]} (expand-like-the-repl ast)\n        {:keys [status tree frontend-metadata log]} result\n        admission [:source :program-in (:t ctx) 0]\n        event-addrs (into #{} (map first) (nth log 1))\n        origins (into #{}\n                      (comp (filter (fn [row] (= :yang/call-site (nth row 3))))\n                            (map first))\n                      frontend-metadata)\n        input-tree (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)\n        final (macro/packet->row-set tree)]\n    (is (= :ok status))\n    (is (not= (:root input-tree) (:root final))\n        \"the twin call really expanded\")\n    (is (seq frontend-metadata))\n    (is (every? (fn [o]\n                  (or (= o admission)\n                      (and (vector? o) (= :expansion (first o))\n                           (contains? event-addrs (second o)))))\n                origins)\n        \"every origin is the admission or names a recorded expansion event\")\n    (is (pos? (count (map-operand-roots ast)))\n        \"the program carries a constructed map through expansion\")))\n'''.replace(\"'\", \"@\").replace(\"@\", chr(39))\n# careful: replace \"'\" back is identity; we only need the raw text as-is\nt = t[:i] + new\np.write_text(t)\nprint(\"part8 rewritten\")\nPYEOF","description":"Rewrite family 6 tests cleanly"}}}
