{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202611190047041ac110d719bd4a25","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A few issues in family 7 to fix:\n1. `ctor-row-id` binding unused/wrong — remove.\n2. In `run-form (read-string ...) {} {})` — run-form takes (form env) two args max; I passed three. Should be `(run-form (read-string (:program payload)) {})` → map of lanes; `(:ast-walker ...)` of the result. Fix: `(get (run-form ...) :ast-walker)`.\n3. `(get (run-form ...) :ast-walker)` — run-form returns lane→value map ✓.\n4. `(read-string ...)` — read-string on cljd/cljs? cljs has cljs.reader/read-string (not in clojure.core read-string? Actually cljs core has read-string via cljs.reader when required? `read-string` is in cljs.core ✓ (it exists). cljd — read-string exists? Risky for portability. Better: store the program as EDN data directly in the payload (already have :program string but re-reading is host-dependent). Cleaner: reconstruct the form structurally in the test (build the same form with list/apply — deterministic across hosts): `(apply hash-map (list (list '- 'x 1) :a (list '- 1 'x) :b))`? The program is `((fn [x] {...}) 1)` — build: `(list (list 'fn ['x] (apply array-map (list '- 'x 1) :a (list '- 1 'x) :b)) 1)`. Wait — CAREFUL: the compiled tree identity depends on the map's insertion order pre-fix... but for the NEW compile (post-fix) insertion doesn't matter. But the FIXTURE's old tree was compiled with array-map insertion [(- x 1) :a, (- 1 x) :b] — for the `not=` root comparison and old-value {0 :b} — new compile canonical → {0 :a} regardless. So structurally building the form with the same insertion order is best. Avoid read-string.\n\nLet me also double check `vm-load-rows` usage: `(ast-walker/vm-load-rows vm rows vm/ast-contract)` returns updated vm; then `(vm/run that-vm)` — vm/run protocol run. In test_utils, run-vm calls `(vm/run vm)`. ✓\n\nAlso `tu/create-vm base-opts` — base-opts has :make-stream, :capability-secret, :primitives, :modules ✓.\n\nFix the issues now.","signature":"d47b521dde45436f9ad6ec90"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"0d1276b7-bcc0-46e6-848f-6f112b2198bb","timestamp":"2026-11-18T16:47:16.220Z","thinking_duration_ms":8879,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202611190047041ac110d719bd4a25","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_94a266b2ff3f4e18b6151e60","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc\")\nt = p.read_text()\nold = '''  (let [payload (legacy-payload)\n        rows (select-keys payload [:root :rows])\n        ctor-row-id (get-in payload [:old-operand-roots 0])\n        recompiled (yang/compile (read-string (:program payload)))]'''\nnew = '''  (let [payload (legacy-payload)\n        rows (select-keys payload [:root :rows])\n        program (list (list (quote fn) [(quote x)]\n                            (apply array-map\n                                   (list (quote -) (quote x) 1) :a\n                                   (list (quote -) 1 (quote x)) :b))\n                      1)\n        recompiled (yang/compile program)]'''\nassert old in t\nt = t.replace(old, new)\nold2 = '''        (is (= (:old-value payload) {0 :b}))\n        (is (not= {0 :b}\n                  (get (run-form (read-string (:program payload)) {} {})\n                       :ast-walker)))))))'''\nnew2 = '''        (is (= (:old-value payload) {0 :b}))\n        (is (not= {0 :b} (:ast-walker (run-form program {})))))))'''\nassert old2 in t\nt = t.replace(old2, new2)\np.write_text(t)\nprint(\"fixed family 7\")\nPYEOF","description":"Fix legacy test program construction"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"3c1a9553-265a-47aa-86dd-0eccdb808e13","timestamp":"2026-11-18T16:47:18.856Z","wire_tool_inputs":{"call_94a266b2ff3f4e18b6151e60":{"command":"python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc\")\nt = p.read_text()\nold = '''  (let [payload (legacy-payload)\n        rows (select-keys payload [:root :rows])\n        ctor-row-id (get-in payload [:old-operand-roots 0])\n        recompiled (yang/compile (read-string (:program payload)))]'''\nnew = '''  (let [payload (legacy-payload)\n        rows (select-keys payload [:root :rows])\n        program (list (list (quote fn) [(quote x)]\n                            (apply array-map\n                                   (list (quote -) (quote x) 1) :a\n                                   (list (quote -) 1 (quote x)) :b))\n                      1)\n        recompiled (yang/compile program)]'''\nassert old in t\nt = t.replace(old, new)\nold2 = '''        (is (= (:old-value payload) {0 :b}))\n        (is (not= {0 :b}\n                  (get (run-form (read-string (:program payload)) {} {})\n                       :ast-walker)))))))'''\nnew2 = '''        (is (= (:old-value payload) {0 :b}))\n        (is (not= {0 :b} (:ast-walker (run-form program {})))))))'''\nassert old2 in t\nt = t.replace(old2, new2)\np.write_text(t)\nprint(\"fixed family 7\")\nPYEOF","description":"Fix legacy test program construction"}}}
