{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_bb76adea1dc8416b9b4d8282","type":"tool_result","content":"440\t     :clj (double x)\n441\t     :cljs (cond (number? x) x\n442\t                 (cbor/float64? x) (.-v ^not-native x)\n443\t                 :else (js/Number x))))\n444\t\n445\t\n446\t(defn float64\n447\t  \"Float content with the value of number `x`: Jing's float64, the form a\n448\t   float keeps in any value that can reach an addressed row or image (a\n449\t   double on the JVM and Dart, the float64 carrier on JS, where a bare\n450\t   integral Number is an integer; dao.jing.cbor.md, Numeric identity). The\n451\t   producer carries float kind; the codec never infers it.\"\n452\t  [x]\n453\t  (cbor/float64 (float-value x)))\n454\t\n455\t\n456\t(defn- callable?\n457\t  \"True when `x` can be applied: a host function, a closure or a\n458\t   continuation. A map is never callable, whatever keys it carries.\"\n459\t  [x]\n460\t  (or (fn? x) (values/closure? x) (values/continuation? x)))\n461\t\n462\t\n463\t(defn- data-map?\n464\t  [x]\n465\t  (map? x))\n466\t\n467\t\n468\t(defn- data-vector?\n469\t  [x]\n470\t  (vector? x))\n471\t\n472\t\n473\t(defn- data-string?\n474\t  [x]\n475\t  (string? x))\n476\t\n477\t\n478\t(defn- ref?\n479\t  \"True when `x` is a stream, cursor or cell reference.\"\n480\t  [x]\n481\t  (and (map? x) (contains? #{:stream-ref :cursor-ref :cell-ref} (:type x))))\n482\t\n483\t\n484\t(defn- data-content=\n485\t  \"True when `a` and `b` have one identity under content addressing:\n486\t   Jing's kind-strict content equality, so every NaN is one value, 0.0 is\n487\t   not -0.0, 1 is not 1.0, and collections recurse. A callable or a\n488\t   reference compares by host `=`, so content addressing never walks it.\"\n489\t  [a b]\n490\t  (or (identical? a b)\n491\t      (if (or (callable? a) (callable? b) (ref? a) (ref? b))\n492\t        (= a b)\n493\t        (cbor/content= a b))))\n494\t\n495\t\n496\t;; =============================================================================\n497\t;; The module\n498\t;; =============================================================================\n499\t\n500\t(def ^:private exports\n501\t  \"`[name arities f]` of every export. `:variadic` means the greatest\n502\t   listed fixed arity extends to further arguments.\"\n503\t  [['count [1] data-count]\n504\t   ['nth [2] data-nth]\n505\t   ['contains? [2] data-contains?]\n506\t   ['dissoc [1 :variadic] data-dissoc]\n507\t   ['disj [1 :variadic] data-disj]\n508\t   ['peek [1] data-peek]\n509\t   ['pop [1] data-pop]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"163d992f-421d-47f2-8d47-659bb7df0b3f","timestamp":"2026-11-18T16:48:35.521Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-fixorder/src/cljc/yin/vm/data.cljc","content":"     :clj (double x)\n     :cljs (cond (number? x) x\n                 (cbor/float64? x) (.-v ^not-native x)\n                 :else (js/Number x))))\n\n\n(defn float64\n  \"Float content with the value of number `x`: Jing's float64, the form a\n   float keeps in any value that can reach an addressed row or image (a\n   double on the JVM and Dart, the float64 carrier on JS, where a bare\n   integral Number is an integer; dao.jing.cbor.md, Numeric identity). The\n   producer carries float kind; the codec never infers it.\"\n  [x]\n  (cbor/float64 (float-value x)))\n\n\n(defn- callable?\n  \"True when `x` can be applied: a host function, a closure or a\n   continuation. A map is never callable, whatever keys it carries.\"\n  [x]\n  (or (fn? x) (values/closure? x) (values/continuation? x)))\n\n\n(defn- data-map?\n  [x]\n  (map? x))\n\n\n(defn- data-vector?\n  [x]\n  (vector? x))\n\n\n(defn- data-string?\n  [x]\n  (string? x))\n\n\n(defn- ref?\n  \"True when `x` is a stream, cursor or cell reference.\"\n  [x]\n  (and (map? x) (contains? #{:stream-ref :cursor-ref :cell-ref} (:type x))))\n\n\n(defn- data-content=\n  \"True when `a` and `b` have one identity under content addressing:\n   Jing's kind-strict content equality, so every NaN is one value, 0.0 is\n   not -0.0, 1 is not 1.0, and collections recurse. A callable or a\n   reference compares by host `=`, so content addressing never walks it.\"\n  [a b]\n  (or (identical? a b)\n      (if (or (callable? a) (callable? b) (ref? a) (ref? b))\n        (= a b)\n        (cbor/content= a b))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The module\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private exports\n  \"`[name arities f]` of every export. `:variadic` means the greatest\n   listed fixed arity extends to further arguments.\"\n  [['count [1] data-count]\n   ['nth [2] data-nth]\n   ['contains? [2] data-contains?]\n   ['dissoc [1 :variadic] data-dissoc]\n   ['disj [1 :variadic] data-disj]\n   ['peek [1] data-peek]\n   ['pop [1] data-pop]","numLines":70,"startLine":440,"totalLines":603}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"call_bb76adea1dc8416b9b4d8282","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
