{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202611190050303206470796d04d7b","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Bug in `all-permutations`: `(if (zero? n) ...)` — my recursion passes `(vec (remove #{i} (range n)))` as n?? Look at line 215: `(if (zero? n)` receiving a VECTOR — because in the mapcat I call `(all-permutations (vec (remove ...)))` — that's the recursive call with the remaining ITEMS not a count. My design was confused: recursion should be over the remaining items directly:\n\n```clojure\n(defn- all-permutations\n  [items]  ; vector\n  (if (empty? items)\n    [[]]\n    (mapcat (fn [i]\n              (map #(into [i] %)\n                   (all-permutations (vec (remove #{i} items)))))\n            items)))\n```\nAnd callers pass `(vec (range n))`. But arity: I call `(all-permutations n)` with a NUMBER in tests. Change signature to take the item count and build items internally... but corpus callers pass entries count and permute entries by INDEX: `(all-permutations n)` returning permutations of indices. Fix:\n\n```clojure\n(defn- index-permutations\n  \"Every ordering of (range n).\"\n  [n]\n  (let [items (vec (range n))]\n    (loop ... )))\n```\nImplement recursively over items:\n\n```clojure\n(defn- permutations-of\n  [items]\n  (if (empty? items)\n    [[]]\n    (mapcat (fn [i]\n              (map (fn [rest-perm] (into [i] rest-perm))\n                   (permutations-of (vec (remove #{i} items)))))\n            items)))\n\n(defn- all-permutations [n] (permutations-of (vec (range n))))\n```\n`remove #{i}` over vector → seq → vec ✓. `into [i] rest-perm` ✓ vector.","signature":"02fc39302e374081a3d5caa3"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"53b487a4-9013-4829-a5d2-856aae0948e4","timestamp":"2026-11-18T16:50:39.168Z","thinking_duration_ms":4635,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202611190050303206470796d04d7b","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_b34cb7e2bcd8406da27e54b0","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc\")\nt = p.read_text()\nold = '''(defn- all-permutations\n  \"Every ordering of (range n), the plain recursive enumeration.\"\n  [n]\n  (if (zero? n)\n    [[]]\n    (mapcat (fn [i]\n              (map #(into [i] %)\n                   (all-permutations (vec (remove #{i} (range n))))))\n            (range n))))'''\nnew = '''(defn- permutations-of\n  \"Every ordering of the items, the plain recursive enumeration.\"\n  [items]\n  (if (empty? items)\n    [[]]\n    (mapcat (fn [i]\n              (map (fn [rest-perm] (into [i] rest-perm))\n                   (permutations-of (vec (remove #{i} items)))))\n            items)))\n\n(defn- all-permutations\n  \"Every ordering of (range n).\"\n  [n]\n  (permutations-of (vec (range n))))'''\nassert old in t\nt = t.replace(old, new)\np.write_text(t)\nprint(\"fixed permutations\")\nPYEOF","description":"Fix permutation enumeration"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"7bb96e34-89a7-424c-9139-0693789afe44","timestamp":"2026-11-18T16:50:41.126Z","wire_tool_inputs":{"call_b34cb7e2bcd8406da27e54b0":{"command":"python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc\")\nt = p.read_text()\nold = '''(defn- all-permutations\n  \"Every ordering of (range n), the plain recursive enumeration.\"\n  [n]\n  (if (zero? n)\n    [[]]\n    (mapcat (fn [i]\n              (map #(into [i] %)\n                   (all-permutations (vec (remove #{i} (range n))))))\n            (range n))))'''\nnew = '''(defn- permutations-of\n  \"Every ordering of the items, the plain recursive enumeration.\"\n  [items]\n  (if (empty? items)\n    [[]]\n    (mapcat (fn [i]\n              (map (fn [rest-perm] (into [i] rest-perm))\n                   (permutations-of (vec (remove #{i} items)))))\n            items)))\n\n(defn- all-permutations\n  \"Every ordering of (range n).\"\n  [n]\n  (permutations-of (vec (range n))))'''\nassert old in t\nt = t.replace(old, new)\np.write_text(t)\nprint(\"fixed permutations\")\nPYEOF","description":"Fix permutation enumeration"}}}
