{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202611190104542b7d63bfb6e74880","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No load error visible. So why only 4 deftests? — OH WAIT. I bet the \"Ran 4 tests\" summary line is cognitect's aggregated summary but tests errored so hard that... no. Let me look: the summary said \"Ran 4 tests containing 80972 assertions. N failures, 2 errors\". Maybe cognitect's -n matched and it ran in ns-load order: map-permutation (346), set-permutation (415), oracle (498), arity-map (650), executable (707), ... — but failures listed only for map-permutation, arity-map, executable (+1 more, maybe set-permutation silently passed?? set-permutation PRE-FIX must FAIL (unsorted!). Unless set-permutation PASSED pre-fix?? Impossible — host set iteration enters operands...\n\nHmm wait — actually! Sets: on the JVM, `(set [a b c])` iteration order is hash-based, same for all my variants of the same elements? DIFFERENT permutations of insertion produce THE SAME JVM hash set (same hashes) → SAME iteration order → same compiled tree pre-fix! And `(apply hash-set ...)` same content → same hash set → same order. So on the JVM pre-fix, set permutation invariance can be GREEN (all permutations converge to one hash order)! The Dart divergence came from Dart's different hashing. So set-permutation passing on JVM pre-fix is EXPECTED — the RED for sets lives on the SORTEDNESS oracle: `ascending?` over element-keys pre-fix — hash order is NOT sorted → must fail... unless element roots happen to be in hash order?? The sized elements `(+ n 0)`, `(+ n 1)`, ... hash order of these FORMS — the compiled element order follows HOST SET iteration of the form values. For it to accidentally be ascending for ALL cases is unlikely...\n\nUnless — set-permutation ERRORED like map-permutation did earlier (PersistentArrayMap.java:75) and I fixed... no wait, the current errors: 2 errors (map-permutation PersistentArrayMap + executable ATransientMap). So set-permutation RAN and PASSED?! and oracle/entry/legacy/token ran and passed?? entry-points-order pre-fix: asserts all entries agree with compile-form reference — pre-fix ALL entries use array-map insertion order of `entry-map-form` — build via map literal `{(tap :k2) ... (tap :k1) ...}` — same insertion on every entry point → same operand vector pre-fix → PASSES pre-fix! (It's a consistency test, not order — green pre-fix is fine.)\n\nlegacy test pre-fix: recompiled root == payload root pre-fix → `(is (not= ...))` FAILS pre-fix... unless it didn't run.\n\nLet me just list which tests RAN by adding... simpler: run with -v? cognitect -v prints each test var. Let me check the runner's var selection — maybe it stops at the first ns error? The 2 errors happened INSIDE tests though.\n\nActually — WAIT. Maybe the answer: \"Ran 4 tests\" — cognitect test-runner counts only FAILED tests?? No — it reports all. Hmm, let me just run with `-v`.","signature":"ea59312be7494cd09fc6f16d"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"617ea7c6-2729-4f40-bc3e-c5b4fffa64a6","timestamp":"2026-11-18T17:05:09.693Z","thinking_duration_ms":12675,"thinking_display":"updates"}
