{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20261119011844315fe2cab268455c","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The MAP LITERAL READER rejects duplicate NaN keys: `{##NaN :left, ##NaN :right}` → \"Duplicate key: NaN\" at READ time (the compiler's map-literal construction DOES use createWithCheck and its equiv says NaN duplicate?? Apparently `createWithCheck` uses `util.equiv` which for numbers uses `Numbers.equal`? Numbers.equiv(nan, nan) → TRUE? In Clojure, `Numbers.equal(##NaN, ##NaN)` is true (equiv for same category uses ==? no...). Actually Clojure `(= ##NaN ##NaN)` → false, but `(== ##NaN ##NaN)` → false too. Hmm — yet the reader throws Duplicate key — because `RT.map` uses `createWithCheck` → checks `equiv` → `Numbers.equal` which does `.equals`? Double.equals(NaN, NaN) is TRUE (Java Double.equals treats NaN==NaN, +0.0≠-0.0)! So map literals with two NaN keys THROW at read, even though `(= nan nan)` is false. Ugh — Clojure's map literal uses Java equals semantics where NaN=NaN and 0.0≠-0.0 — the OPPOSITE of `=`.\n\nSo: build the map at RUNTIME: `(array-map ##NaN :left ##NaN :right)`? `array-map` → createWithCheck → same throw! `(hash-map ...)` same. BUT `(zipmap [##NaN ##NaN] [:left :right])`? zipmap assoc's — assoc uses equiv (= semantics) → NaN≠NaN → both stay! Or `(into {} [[##NaN :left] [##NaN :right]])` — into conj on map → uses equiv(=) → keeps both ✓. Or explicit: `(assoc {} ##NaN :left ##NaN :right)` ✓ keeps both.\n\nUse `(into {} [[##NaN :left] [##NaN :right]])` — wait `into {}` of vector pairs — conj [k v] onto map — map conj on VECTOR entries uses `(get m k)`→ equiv → NaN not found → assoc ✓ both stay. Count 2 ✓.\n\nFor sets: `#{##NaN ##NaN}` reader — same check? Set literals also createWithCheck → throw. Build `(into #{} [##NaN ##NaN])` → disj/conj with equiv → 2 elements ✓.\n\nFix the three NaN constructions.","signature":"87544a50c5e8412da13f1706"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"c9cc7c2d-c114-4755-8b03-7b9475dd5851","timestamp":"2026-11-18T17:18:56.189Z","thinking_duration_ms":8273,"thinking_display":"updates"}
