{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20261119012244ecb801677c964834","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Two clear bugs:\n\n1. **colliding/executable**: `Unable to resolve symbol: n` — the stack lane's run: my colliding test calls `trace-of (inserter es) {'n 1}` — env `{'n 1}` — env keys: I wrote `{'n 1}`? Let me check — earlier quote-mangling! `{'n' 1}` got fixed to `{'n 1}` ✓... but the error says resolve n fails in debruijn.stack step1 — env not applied for the STACK lane? In call_test the runners pass `opts` including env? call_test's runners don't use env at all. The stack/register VMs — do they honor :env from opts? `dvm/create-vm image (assoc opts :contract ...)` — create-vm for stack machine — does it read :env? Maybe stack machine expects initial env differently! The walker resolved n fine (ast-walker create-vm :env ✓); semantic lane: `semantic/create-vm opts` + load — resolves? The error came from stack lane. If stack/register machines don't support env lookup, my env-based tests break there.\n\nLet me check dvm/create-vm handling of :env.\n\n2. **legacy line 973**: `apply` over `program` — line 973 is `(apply array-map (list (quote -) ...))` — `(apply array-map (list 'x) 1)`?? My program build:\n```clojure\nprogram (list (list 'fn ['x] (apply array-map (list '- 'x 1) :a (list '- 1 'x) :b)) 1)\n```\n`(apply array-map (list '- 'x 1) :a ...)` — apply's LAST arg must be a seq; I passed multiple args where only the last is seq: `(apply array-map (list '- 'x 1) :a (list '- 1 'x) :b)` — apply takes (f args*) with last seq — here last arg is `:b` — a KEYWORD → \"Don't know how to create ISeq from Keyword\". Fix: `(apply array-map [(list '- 'x 1) :a (list '- 1 'x) :b])`.\n\nFor #1: check dvm/create-vm :env support.","signature":"65415a021fb643cdb22e5560"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_