{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20261119012624bc40cc4bf6fb415b","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The `boom` host exception propagates OUT of `vm/run` (not converted to a VM error) — expected: \"An exception or transfer of control during an operand prevents the later evaluations\" — the exception unwinds through. My test must CATCH it per lane: wrap the lane run in try/catch and record the log regardless. Restructure `trace-of` to catch exceptions per lane and include them:\n\n```clojure\n(defn- trace-of [form env]\n  (let [ast (yang/compile form)\n        log (atom [])\n        env (assoc env 'tap ...)\n        run (fn [lane]\n              (reset! log [])\n              (try\n                {:value (vm/value (run-lane lane ast env))}\n                (catch #?(:clj Exception :cljs :default :cljd Object) e\n                  {:error e})\n                (finally... hmm need log after\n```\nCareful: log read AFTER the run whether or not it threw:\n\n```clojure\n(fn [lane]\n  (reset! log [])\n  (let [result (try {:value (vm/value (run-lane lane ast env))}\n                    (catch #?(:clj Exception, :cljs :default, :cljd Object) e\n                      {:raised (ex-data e)}))]\n    (assoc result :log @log)))\n```\nNote the walker's throw of the host ex-info propagates; ex-data preserved. For stack/register lanes the exception may surface differently (as ex-info with data or wrapped) — assert log prefix and `:raised` presence on at least the walker lane. My assertion: log is prefix ([:early :early-v] or []) ✓ plus at least one lane raised. Update the failure test accordingly.","signature":"ccdb55fbd1ed451588a84300"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"57135829-cbbf-4405-b370-521fa7500cd0","timestamp":"2026-11-18T17:26:33.365Z","thinki