59189(:a), 3ddc0d87]] — WAIT :b first?? Independent sorted: :b-root < :a-root ✓ (398... < b18...). fa79133b = standalone compile of `(+ n 2)`, 3ddc0d87 = standalone `(+ n 1)`. ACTUAL pairs: [398f68e0, 690acf7e], [b1859189, 88210be4]. So the EMITTED value for :b has root 690acf7e but the standalone-compiled `(+ n 2)` has root fa79133b! DIFFERENT compiled content for the same source form!\n\nWhy? In-tree compile of `(+ n 2)` inside the map: tail? = false, env {} — standalone `yang/compile` of `(+ n 2)` — SAME env... but the difference: annotate-call-sites marks STANDALONE compile (top-level compile-form wraps with *call-site-finalizing* and annotates) — the mark `:yang/call-site 1` goes on the :application node — projection DROPS :yang/* keys ✓ same row... \n\nHmm, but WAIT — compile-form's metadata merge: `(vary-meta ast merge (dissoc m ::fn-loop))` — the FORM `(+ n 2)` carries READER metadata (line/column from my test file)! Standalone vs in-tree — same meta. What differs...\n\nOH! I bet it's `:yang/site` — safepoint marks! `annotate-call-sites` or tails adds `:yang/site` marks (safepoint) — those are \"node metadata\" that projection... \"sym slots lose all metadata; data/key payloads lose reader positions\" — but `:yang/site` is a NODE KEY not metadata — does the row include it? The grammar for :application has only [operator operands tail?] — :yang/site dropped from ROWS ✓ but the ENCODER hashes... I'm projecting with vm/ast->semantic-bytecode — node keys beyond grammar dropped ✓.\n\nHmm — so what differs? Let me just compute: standalone `(root-of (yang/compile (list '+ 'n 2)))` vs the in-tree operand. Maybe the in-tree child has `:tail?`?? No — children compile with tail?=false.\n\nAH WAIT — I see it! `annotate-call-sites` runs at the TOP of compile-form (the collection emitter's parent). The standalone compile ALSO annotates. BUT — the ORDER of operations: in-tree, the compiled child nodes get their `:yang/call-site` marks when the OWNING compile-form (the top one) walks. Standalone: annotate-call-sites wraps JUST that subtree. Both end with marks. Same projection.\n\nHmm — different theory: the SAFEDOINT `:yang/site` — check `annotate-call-sites`... Actually, easier: probe directly. Compute both roots in a scratch and diff the ASTs. Let me run a quick scratch.","signature":"11928c7de2ad40b094386207"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"c54ee45b-3e69-4385-99e0-594598d2d91a","timestamp":"2026-11-18T17:40:36.399Z","thinking_duration_ms":17263,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202611190140163039eac68bde4626","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_deb7a1ce06604b0698145b3f","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nPath(\"test/fixorder_tmp_diag_test.cljc\").write_text('''(ns fixorder-tmp-diag-test\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is]]\n            [yang.clojure :as yang]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]))\n\n(deftest diag-roots-test\n  (let [form {:a (list (quote +) (quote n) 1)}\n        ast (yang/compile form)\n        ctor (first\n               (into []\n                     (comp (filter map?)\n                           (filter (fn [n]\n                                     (and (= :application (:type n))\n                                          (= (quote assoc) (get-in n [:operator :name]))))))\n                     (tree-seq coll? seq ast)))\n        in-tree (nth (:operands ctor) 2)\n        standalone (yang/compile (list (quote +) (quote n) 1))]\n    (println :in-tree-root (:root (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode in-tree)))\n    (println :standalone-root (:root (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode standalone)))\n    (println :in-tree (pr-str in-tree))\n    (println :standalone (pr-str standalone))\n    (println :in-tree-rows (pr-str (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode in-tree)))\n    (println :standalone-rows (pr-str (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode standalone))))))\n''')\nprint(\"ok\")\nPYEOF\nclojure -M:test -n fixorder-tmp-diag-test 2>&1 | grep -A2 \"Testing\" | head -20","description":"Diagnose in-tree vs standalone child roots","timeout":600000}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"e7254532-2d4b-41c3-bdf6-fba1f569123c","timestamp":"2026-11-18T17:40:39.484Z","wire_tool_inputs":{"call_deb7a1ce06604b0698145b3f":{"command":"python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nPath(\"test/fixorder_tmp_diag_test.cljc\").write_text('''(ns fixorder-tmp-diag-test\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is]]\n            [yang.clojure :as yang]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]))\n\n(deftest diag-roots-test\n  (let [form {:a (list (quote +) (quote n) 1)}\n        ast (yang/compile form)\n        ctor (first\n               (into []\n                     (comp (filter map?)\n                           (filter (fn [n]\n                                     (and (= :application (:type n))\n                                          (= (quote assoc) (get-in n [:operator :name]))))))\n                     (tree-seq coll? seq ast)))\n        in-tree (nth (:operands ctor) 2)\n        standalone (yang/compile (list (quote +) (quote n) 1))]\n    (println :in-tree-root (:root (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode in-tree)))\n    (println :standalone-root (:root (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode standalone)))\n    (println :in-tree (pr-str in-tree))\n    (println :standalone (pr-str standalone))\n    (println :in-tree-rows (pr-str (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode in-tree)))\n    (println :standalone-rows (pr-str (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode standalone))))))\n''')\nprint(\"ok\")\nPYEOF\nclojure -M:test -n fixorder-tmp-diag-test 2>&1 | grep -A2 \"Testing\" | head -20","description":"Diagnose in-tree vs standalone child roots","timeout":600000}}}
