tion. The ruling's corpus wants \"quoted collection keys\" — but TWO MUTUALLY-EQUAL keys can't coexist. FIX THE CORPUS: make the two quoted keys host-UNEQUAL — e.g. quote [1 2] and quote ^:sem [1 3] (different VALUES, one with meta). That preserves \"semantic metadata in quoted keys\" coverage without the equality collapse.\n\nSame lesson for the oracle's \"semantic metadata stays content\" test — it used different keys already ([quoted-meta] vs :plain) ✓ fine.\n\nSo: update map-corpus :heterogeneous-keys — change quoted-meta-key to `(list 'quote (with-meta [1 2] {:sem true}))` → make value [2 3] distinct? But I WANT same-value-with-meta vs plain to assert metadata-is-content — that's the ORACLE test (different roots across two maps) ✓ already there. Corpus needs distinct values: use `(with-meta [1 2] {:sem true})` AND plain `[2 3]`? The corpus's quoted-pair-key [1 2] and quoted-meta-key — change meta key's vector to [3 4]: `(list 'quote (with-meta [3 4] {:sem true}))`.","signature":"11a4b7c505234d77ae9c2bf4"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"1a1063b2-41bf-4073-bba3-dc6f367a682c","timestamp":"2026-11-18T18:09:01.189Z","thinking_duration_ms":21411,"thinking_display":"updates"}
