{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202611190215590eb6e828c2e94593","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"1. **Executable 732**: my \"no duplication\" block hardcoded `[:k :v :k2 :v2]` — but the canonical order puts :k2's pair FIRST (log [:k2 :v2 :k :v]). Derive expected like the first block: `(vec (mapcat identity (sort-by pair-key ...)))` — or simpler, accept both orderings derived from the independent builder. Fix: build expected from sorted pairs of the entry forms.\n\n2. **Entry-points 842**: roots-a not all-equal — the unit-opts program contains MULTIPLE constructed maps (the arity maps from `def m` compile? unit-forms = `[(def m entry-map-form)]` — under unit-opts with `:outcomes`, lowering wraps def... the map-operand-roots list contains: the entry map (5 roots) + OTHER constructed maps (yang.call 2-pair maps from the convention preamble — [seed :yang.call/reason ...]) — these differ from each other (different single-pair maps). `(apply = roots-a)` wrongly demands all constructed maps in the unit agree. Fix: compare each convention entry's map-roots as a SET / or find the map with the entry's signature (5 operands) — assert the 5-operand ctor identical across the two entries and ascending. Simpler: `(is (= (set roots-a) (set roots-b)))` + every 5-operand ctor ascending + the 5-operand ctor EQUAL across entries.","signature":"dc63291b8a5a42768ffb5a43"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"693df7f1-31a7-4d9e-bb8a-757667d688cc","timestamp":"2026-11-18T18:16:08.802Z","thinking_duration_ms":4655,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202611190215590eb6e828c2e94593","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_44ed3fe999134f3082dfe781","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc\")\nt = p.read_text()\nold = \"\"\"  (testing \"no duplication: every occurrence evaluates exactly once\"\n    (let [traces (trace-of {(list 'tap :k) (list 'tap :v)\n                            (list 'tap :k2) (list 'tap :v2)}\n                           {})]\n      (doseq [[lane {:keys [log]}] traces]\n        (is (= (vec (mapcat identity [[:k :v] [:k2 :v2]])) log)\n            (str lane)))))\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"  (testing \"no duplication: every occurrence evaluates exactly once\"\n    (let [entries [[(list 'tap :k) (list 'tap :v)]\n                   [(list 'tap :k2) (list 'tap :v2)]]\n          tap-arg (fn [form] (get-in (yang/compile form) [:operands 0 :value]))\n          ordered (sort-by (fn [[k v]]\n                             [(root-of (yang/compile-form k false {}))\n                              (root-of (yang/compile-form v false {}))])\n                           jing/canonical-compare entries)\n          expected (into [] (mapcat (fn [[k v]] [(tap-arg k) (tap-arg v)]))\n                         ordered)\n          traces (trace-of (apply array-map (into [] (mapcat identity) entries)) {})]\n      (is (= 4 (count expected)))\n      (doseq [[lane {:keys [log]}] traces]\n        (is (= expected log) (str lane)))))\"\"\"\nassert old in t; t = t.replace(old, new)\nold = \"\"\"    (let [unit-forms [(list (quote def) (quote m) entry-map-form)]\n          asts {:compile-program-unit (yang/compile-program unit-forms true yang/unit-opts)\n                :lower-unit (yang/lower-unit unit-forms)}\n          roots-a (map-operand-roots (:compile-program-unit asts))\n          roots-b (map-operand-roots (:lower-unit asts))]\n      (is (pos? (count roots-a)))\n      (is (apply = roots-a) \"the unit's constructed maps agree\")\n      (is (= (vec roots-a) (vec roots-b)))\n      (is (every? #(ascending? (pair-keys %))\n                  (map-constructors (:lower-unit asts))))))\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"    (let [unit-forms [(list (quote def) (quote m) entry-map-form)]\n          asts {:compile-program-unit (yang/compile-program unit-forms true yang/unit-opts)\n                :lower-unit (yang/lower-unit unit-forms)}\n          ;; the entry's own map is the 5-operand constructor (seed + 2\n          ;; pairs); the convention preamble adds its own single-pair maps\n          entry-map-roots (fn [ast]\n                            (into #{}\n                                  (map child-roots)\n                                  (filter #(= 5 (count (:operands %)))\n                                          (map-constructors ast))))\n          roots-a (entry-map-roots (:compile-program-unit asts))\n          roots-b (entry-map-roots (:lower-unit asts))]\n      (is (= 1 (count roots-a)))\n      (is (= roots-a roots-b))\n      (is (every? #(ascending? (pair-keys %))\n                  (map-constructors (:lower-unit asts))))))\"\"\"\nassert old in t; t = t.replace(old, new)\np.write_text(t)\nprint(\"residuals fixed\")\nPYEOF","description":"Fix no-dup expectation and entry-map selection"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"db57d746-7a8b-469b-b1a3-157a36a64588","timestamp":"2026-11-18T18:16:14.572Z","wire_tool_inputs":{"call_44ed3fe999134f3082dfe781":{"command":"python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc\")\nt = p.read_text()\nold = \"\"\"  (testing \"no duplication: every occurrence evaluates exactly once\"\n    (let [traces (trace-of {(list 'tap :k) (list 'tap :v)\n                            (list 